{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"f9d6360cdbe4e684885a065d153f9519b45350be423322311962a7bc8fd37517","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reproduced the shard runner's exact conditions — compiled binary, run from `/tmp` — and it passes now. Pushing:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SAiHjmtfEs194UsfUGYyGU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix && rm -f /tmp/clitest; git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -m \"test: resolve the source guard relative to its own file, not the cwd\n\nWindows shard 7 was the only failure, and it was my guard rather than the\nfix. The Windows runner executes PRECOMPILED test binaries from a temp\ndirectory, so reading a bare \\\"memory_cmd.go\\\" finds nothing; every other\nplatform runs tests with the package directory as cwd and never noticed.\n\nResolved via runtime.Caller(0) now, and it SKIPS rather than fails if the\nsource genuinely is not shipped alongside, because a guard that cannot read\nits subject should say so instead of reporting a defect that is not there.\n\nReproduced the runner's conditions before and after: go test -c, then the\nbinary executed from /tmp. Fails on the old form, passes on this one.\" && git push origin HEAD:fix/distill-pipeline 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]|cannot lock|another git\" | tail -2","description":"Push the shard fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
