{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","prNumber":426,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/426","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:13:48.545Z"}
{"parentUuid":"86f0d104-2252-41f1-8fe7-4bb773070830","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14908287 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1ff68dd8-8de3-4b8f-99ca-50b124aa9600","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:13:48.444Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14908287 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"1ff68dd8-8de3-4b8f-99ca-50b124aa9600","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01BHtZAhiprcRXMGRcy9ACCq","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b6803010-ff35-49f2-bd2e-3573d64a780a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:14:05.157Z","session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"b6803010-ff35-49f2-bd2e-3573d64a780a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgGEM5aZGV5rB8sN3Q7gw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**PR #426 is ready for tonight's release.** Checks passed, findings passed, up to date, mergeable. Only `Approvals` — yours.\n\n## What's in it\n\n**COR-2175 — the daemon was blocking itself.** The watch tick queued reconciliation, launched the memory worker detached, then ran a refresh needing the same `write.lock`. The worker always won; refresh timed out, logged `brain_locked`, **skipped all agent work including distill**, and didn't advance its cursor. 368 of 369 observed failures followed a reconciliation in the same tick — so on any repo with an active session, daemon distill effectively never ran. The tick now waits for the lock to clear.\n\n**COR-2177 — distill paid twice for every merged session.** The cache is keyed `branch/session`, and export deliberately copies merged sessions onto the default branch, so every copy was a full cache miss. Reuse is now content-addressed across branches — sound because the hashes *are* content hashes.\n\n**COR-2176 — `watch.log` was unreadable.** No clock, no repo. Stamped at the writer so a line added later can't forget it.\n\n## Four mistakes I made, and how they surfaced\n\nI want these visible rather than buried, because three were caught by CI and not by me:\n\n1. **The first fix re-execed the test binary.** I waited on the *process* via `os.Executable()` — inside a test binary, that's the test binary, spawned and waited on. 36 tests stub `memoryWorkerLaunch` precisely to stop that; my new seam bypassed all of them. Now it waits on the **lock**, behind the seam they already stub.\n\n2. **It then timed CI out at 30m42s.** My wait treated *every* lock error as \"still held\", so tests with unlockable brain dirs each sat through the full 90s budget. That failure was a **timeout, not an assertion** — I'd have misread it without checking the timestamps. Only `brain_locked` is waited out now; the suite is back to 322s.\n\n3. **Two of my own tests were vacuous.** One measured elapsed time *after* joining the goroutine that released the lock, so it passed against a no-op. The other used a missing directory as its \"unlockable\" case — the lock just *creates* it and succeeds, so it passed against the exact bug it was written for. Both only showed up under weakening.\n\n4. **A source-text guard failed twice on Windows shard 7** — first cwd, then CRLF, which my own notes already warn about. I proved the mechanism before fixing it the second time instead of guessing again.\n\nFive weakening checks now hold: removing the settle call, making settle return immediately, dropping the contention filter, blanking the log stamp, removing the cross-branch half of the reuse decision.\n\n## For tonight\n\nApprove **#426**, then cut **COR-2157**. The stray tags are gone, so tagging is clean. **#350** should be closed or rebuilt docs-only — it exists to pre-integrate a stack that's already landed.\n\nOne caveat worth knowing before you tag: anyone who upgrades the brain before the `entire` CLI hits the `connect` failure I saw tonight — the brain calls `entire repo view --json`, which older CLIs reject. No ticket yet; say the word and I'll file it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":915255,"output_tokens":1070,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1070,"cache_read_input_tokens":915255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bf1a730e-9d80-456e-83c7-ed486c924bc9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGEM57HNDtCuCJ24nnMn","requestRef":"7b357b22-70a3-4f81-b7f9-f4a7fcf1af77","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"173a8d81-e2a3-4ec9-a32f-6235ec20ae00","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:14:05.156Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
