{"parentUuid":"2475e6eb-ec7d-46c3-8a03-efc178dd351c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgGEz2cFL5vzjaNtcWC1b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawning an independent reviewer — giving it the code and the issues, not my conclusions:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":915699,"output_tokens":1564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1564,"cache_read_input_tokens":915699,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c0d26112-2a6c-476a-8237-2887cf66f33c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGEyzAQETdYoKbohSFGF","requestRef":"59a61ab8-fc8d-4244-8837-71c0a29bf611","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"f5088442-4d47-4b91-b942-73872997a241","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:22:30.569Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"f5088442-4d47-4b91-b942-73872997a241","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgGEz2cFL5vzjaNtcWC1b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Hw9Rs9Ba5dXJZELwEGqgU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Independent review of PR 426","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Adversarially review a Go change in the worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix (branch fix/distill-pipeline, repo entireio/entire-brain). Default to REFUTED: only report a defect you can point at in the actual code.\n\nScope — review `git diff origin/main...HEAD` in that worktree. Changed files:\n  internal/cli/memory_cmd.go\n  internal/cli/distill_cmd.go\n  internal/cli/watch.go\n  internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go              (new)\n  internal/cli/watch_worker_lock_race_test.go   (new)\n  internal/cli/distill_merged_session_reuse_test.go (new)\n  internal/cli/watch_log_prefix_test.go         (new)\n\nWhat the change is SUPPOSED to do (from the tickets, not from me):\n1. COR-2175: the `workspace watch` daemon tick queued long-term memory reconciliation, launched `memory worker --once` DETACHED, then ran a refresh needing the same brain write.lock. The worker held it 11-16s, refresh's timeout was shorter, so the tick logged brain_locked and skipped all agent work including distill.\n2. COR-2177: the distill cache is keyed branch/session. Session export deliberately copies a merged feature-branch session onto the default branch, so each copy was a cache miss and the same transcript was re-sent to the agent once per branch.\n3. COR-2176: watch.log lines had no timestamp and no repo.\n\nQuestions I want answered, with evidence:\n- Correctness of `memoryWorkerSettle` in memory_cmd.go: can it spin, block a tick indefinitely, busy-loop, or swallow a real failure? Is the `brain_locked:` substring test a sound way to detect contention — what else could produce or omit that string? Is the 90s budget reachable in a bad case and what happens then?\n- Correctness of `chunkSetForSession` / `distillChunksAlreadyDone` in distill_cmd.go. THE CRITICAL RISK: a chunk wrongly treated as already-distilled is a chunk whose facts never get written. Can the key matching ever match the wrong session? Consider url.PathEscape behaviour, branch names containing escaped slashes or \"/\", empty branch, the duplicate-disambiguated third key segment, and session ids that escape to the same string.\n- `watchLogPrefixWriter` in watch_log_prefix.go: is the io.Writer contract honoured (return value, partial writes, errors)? What happens on a write not ending in a newline, an empty write, or interleaved concurrent writes from different goroutines?\n- Do the NEW tests actually hold their claims, or can any pass while the code is wrong? Try to find a test that would stay green against a broken implementation.\n- Anything in the diff that could behave differently on Windows.\n\nDo NOT run the full `internal/cli` suite (it takes ~5 min). You may run targeted `go test ./internal/cli/ -run <pattern>` and `go build`/`go vet`. Use `env -u FORCE_COLOR` and `GOMAXPROCS=2` on any go command. Use rtk where it saves tokens.\n\nReport caveman-ultra compressed: one line per finding, `file:line — defect — why it matters`. Rank by severity. If you find nothing in a category, say so in three words. No preamble, no summary of what the code does, no praise."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_read_input_tokens":915699,"output_tokens":1564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1564,"cache_read_input_tokens":915699,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016Hw9Rs9Ba5dXJZELwEGqgU":{"description":"Independent review of PR 426","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Adversarially review a Go change in the worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix (branch fix/distill-pipeline, repo entireio/entire-brain). Default to REFUTED: only report a defect you can point at in the actual code.\n\nScope — review `git diff origin/main...HEAD` in that worktree. Changed files:\n  internal/cli/memory_cmd.go\n  internal/cli/distill_cmd.go\n  internal/cli/watch.go\n  internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go              (new)\n  internal/cli/watch_worker_lock_race_test.go   (new)\n  internal/cli/distill_merged_session_reuse_test.go (new)\n  internal/cli/watch_log_prefix_test.go         (new)\n\nWhat the change is SUPPOSED to do (from the tickets, not from me):\n1. COR-2175: the `workspace watch` daemon tick queued long-term memory reconciliation, launched `memory worker --once` DETACHED, then ran a refresh needing the same brain write.lock. The worker held it 11-16s, refresh's timeout was shorter, so the tick logged brain_locked and skipped all agent work including distill.\n2. COR-2177: the distill cache is keyed branch/session. Session export deliberately copies a merged feature-branch session onto the default branch, so each copy was a cache miss and the same transcript was re-sent to the agent once per branch.\n3. COR-2176: watch.log lines had no timestamp and no repo.\n\nQuestions I want answered, with evidence:\n- Correctness of `memoryWorkerSettle` in memory_cmd.go: can it spin, block a tick indefinitely, busy-loop, or swallow a real failure? Is the `brain_locked:` substring test a sound way to detect contention — what else could produce