{"parentUuid":"5fb82782-ee64-4ae3-ae53-ef21248fe406","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgGF9JaRvfratu2FmSxjG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's where things stand while the reviewer finishes.\n\n## Trail review — clean\n\nTrail **#337** gates:\n\n| gate | |\n|---|---|\n| `findings` | **passed — `finding_count: 0`** |\n| `checks` | passed |\n| `up_to_date` | passed |\n| `approvals` | ❌ yours |\n\nWorth being precise: that zero is a **real** zero. The gate reports `finding_count: 0` explicitly, whereas gates that never ran report `None` — a distinction that has previously fooled me into reading \"no review happened\" as \"nothing found\". The agent review ran and found nothing to fix.\n\n## Merge safety against current main\n\nMain has moved 4 commits ahead (COR-2203, COR-2202, COR-2212 and a command-state audit), and one of them touches `watch.go`, which I also changed. I checked rather than assumed:\n\n- merges **clean**\n- merged result **builds**\n- all the new tests **pass** against it\n\n## Still outstanding\n\nThe independent reviewer is still running. I gave it the code and the three tickets, told it to default to *refuted*, and pointed it specifically at the risk that actually matters here — **a chunk wrongly treated as already-distilled is a chunk whose facts never get written** — plus the lock-settle's failure modes, the `io.Writer` contract, and whether any of my new tests could stay green against a broken implementation.\n\nI'll report whatever it finds, fix anything real, and merge only after that. I won't merge on the strength of my own review of my own code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":304,"cache_read_input_tokens":922201,"output_tokens":499,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tie