stop CI timing out never runs on the Windows shard. Nothing else in the diff is platform-sensitive (`bytes.Split` on `\\n` keeps `\\r` inside the line; `isLockBusy` maps `ERROR_LOCK_VIOLATION`/`ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION`, so the `brain_locked:` substring test holds there).\n  \n  **Refuted** (checked, no defect): settle cannot spin or busy-loop (bounded deadline + ctx check on both exits); the `brain_locked:` substring is a sound contention test (`fileLockTimeoutError` `filelock.go:170-172` is the only producer and every non-contention path returns a differently-prefixed error); the 90s budget is reachable and simply proceeds; `ps.chunks[:0]` aliasing does **not** desync `ps.chunkHashes` (hashes are deliberately the full list, `:175-178`, and `:1465` records the full list only when no chunk failed); `url.PathEscape` escapes `/` so branch and session are always single segments; empty branch and empty session id are both handled.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"VERIFIED: `go build ./...` OK, `go vet ./internal/cli` OK, all 10 new tests pass. Three throwaway probe tests were added, run, and deleted; `git status --porcelain` clean.\n\n**CRITICAL**\n1. `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:640` (+ call site `:346`) — cross-branch chunk reuse **drops facts on the destination branch**. Facts are stored in a **per-branch file**: `internal/cli/facts.go:115-122` `factsBranchRelDir(branch)` → `facts/<slug>-<sha>/facts.ndjson`, written by `writeFacts(brainDir, branch, byBranch[branch])` (`distill_cmd.go:1216`), loaded per-branch (`:1146`), never merged across branches. Chunk hashes are branch-free (`distillChunkHashes` `:683` = sha256(salt+text)), and `resolveDistillBranch` (`:1861`) keeps `feature/x` and `main` as distinct branches. So: session distilled on `feature/x` in run 1, merged+copied onto `main`, run 2 → `chunkSetForSession` returns every chunk → `ps.chunks` emptied → the `for chunkIdx, chunk := range ps.chunks` loop at `:1373` never runs → **zero facts land in `byBranch[\"main\"]`** → and `:1462-1465` then writes `newCache.Sessions[mainKey]` + the FULL hash list, marking it done permanently. The comment at `:637-638` (\"its facts are already in the store, whichever branch paid for it\") is false — the store is branch-partitioned. This is exactly the failure mode the code's own comment at `:650-652` calls worse than paying twice, and it is the central mechanism of the COR-2177 fix.\n\n**HIGH**\n2. `internal/cli/memory_cmd.go:134-137` — **settle is a no-op in the production path**; COR-2175 is not fixed. `memoryWorkerLaunch` → `launchDetachedSelf` returns at `command.Start()`; the child must then do Go runtime init + cobra + `resolveSessionsBrain` (git) + `resolveLocalTargetRepoDir` (git) + tombstones + `acquireMemoryCoordinator` before it touches write.lock. Settle's **first** poll fires microseconds later, finds the lock free, and returns. Measured probe: settle returned in **289µs** while the \"worker\" took the lock at **+51ms**; warm `entire-brain --help` alone is ~10ms (cold 380ms). The loop only waits if the lock is *already* held at the first poll.\n3. `internal/cli/memory_cmd.go:296` + `internal/cli/watch.go:740` — the settle fires on the **wrong side** in the second `\"watch\"` caller. `watchDeterministicRefreshComponents` calls `runRefresh` at `:722` and only then `reconcileMemoryAndLaunch(..., \"watch\")` at `:740`, so the ≤90s wait buys nothing there. Worse, that function is reached from **`internal/cli/setup.go:1852`** → interactive `setup` can now stall 90s. And a watch tick calls reconcile (`watch.go:486`) *and* refresh (`:492`→`:667`→`:740`), so each tick can pay the budget twice; `workspace.go:518` fans out serially → worst case N×180s per pass against a 5m interval.\n\n**MEDIUM**\n4. `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:653` — the segment index is wrong for duplicate-disambiguated keys. `distillSessionCacheKeyFor` (`:2440`) builds `escape(branch)/escape(discriminator)/escape(session)`, i.e. the session is `parts[2]`, not `parts[1]`; the comment at `:648-649` has the layout backwards. Verified probe: key `\"main/CKPT/S1\"` → `chunkSetForSession(\"S1\")` = `map[]` (own session never reused) and `chunkSetForSession(\"CKPT\")` = `map[h:true]` — **a different session whose id equals another entry's checkpoint id gets a false \"already distilled\"**, i.e. finding 1's failure mode by key collision. Low real-world probability only because checkpoint ids and session ids happen to be different ID spaces.\n5. `internal/cli/watch.go:197` vs `internal/cli/workspace.go:518` — COR-2176 is **not fixed for the daemon**. Only single-repo `runWatch` wraps the writer; `runWorkspaceWatchPass` passes raw `cmd.OutOrStdout()` into `watchTick`, so the workspace fan-out — the exact case the rationale cites — still logs bare, unattributed lines. Also every `cmd.ErrOrStderr()` warning (`watch.go:488,501,738,742`) and every sub-command's output (`sub.SetOut(cmd.OutOrStdout())` at `:720,:773,:798`) bypasses the prefix, so watch.log interleaves stamped and unstamped lines.\n6. Tests that stay green against a broken implementation: `watch_worker_lock_race_test.go:25` pre-holds the lock before calling settle, so it **passes against the shipped no-op** (proved by probe 2) — it never exercises launch→settle ordering, which is the real sequence; `:88-137` is a source-string grep that `t.Skip`s when the file is unreadable and cannot see semantics; `:54-68` asserts only an upper bound (green for `func(){}`); `distill_merged_session_reuse_test.go` never builds a duplicate-disambiguated key (so finding 4 is untested) and nothing covers whether facts are still written for the destination branch (finding 1).\n\n**LOW**\n7. `internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go:42` — `Write(nil)`/`Write([]byte{})` emits a bare `\"\\n\"` (verified). An empty write must write nothing.\n8. `internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go:38-61` — writer is stateless, so a write not ending in `\\n` leaves the line open and the next write injects its prefix mid-line. Verified: `\"…no-newline2026-10-21T04:05:06Z repo tail\\n\"`.\n9. `internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go:57` — returns `(0, err)` though the underlying writer may already have written bytes; misreports progress (contract-legal, still wrong). No mutex, but safe today since each `Write` is exactly one underlying `Write`.\n10. `internal/cli/watch_log_prefix.go:44-50` — a blank line yields `\"<stamp> repo \\n\"` (bare prefix + trailing space); verified.\n11. `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1799-1832` — `buildDistillPlanContext` applies **no** chunk reuse at all, so `--dry-run` will still print \"209 of 209 uncached\" after this change: the metric quoted as COR-2177's evidence (`:633`) is not what the fix moves, and dry-run now diverges further from the real run.\n12. `internal/cli/watch.go:486,740` — still the literal `\"watch\"`, not the new `memoryTriggerWatch`; only the source-grep test keeps them in sync.\n13. `internal/cli/memory_cmd.go:137` — each settle poll calls `acquireFileLock`, which does `os.MkdirAll` + a 10ms-interval open/flock retry loop internally, so a full 90s budget is ~9k fs cycles, not ~225; each *successful* probe also rewrites `write.lock.owner` (`filelock.go:342`) with the watch pid for a lock held microseconds.\n\n**Windows** — one gap only: `watch_worker_lock_race_test.go:147` needs `os.Symlink`, which is privileged on Windows → `t.Skip`, so the guard that exists to stop CI timing out never runs on the Windows shard. Nothing else in the diff is platform-sensitive (`bytes.Split` on `\\n` keeps `\\r` inside the line; `isLockBusy` maps `ERROR_LOCK_VIOLATION`/`ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION`, so the `brain_locked:` substring test holds there).\n\n**Refuted** (checked, no defect): settle cannot spin or busy-loop (bounded deadline + ctx check on both exits); the `brain_locked:` substring is a sound contention test (`fileLockTimeoutError` `filelock.go:170-172` is the only producer and every non-contention path returns a differently-prefixed error); the 90s budget is reachable and simply proceeds; `ps.chunks[:0]` aliasing does **not** desync `ps.chunkHashes` (hashes are deliberately the full list, `:175-178`, and `:1465` records the full list only when no chunk failed); `url.PathEscape` escapes `/` so branch and session are always single segments; empty branch and empty session id are both handled."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
