{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"c29413e94c32f9f973521a8f81c9b65aa638404385d831ecd74f62827186c75a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Both answers, then the fix.\n\n## 1. Are the two related? No.\n\n| | ashtom's first message | ashtom's second message (the one you care about) |\n|---|---|---|\n| repo | `entire-graph` | `entire-brain` |\n| subsystem | `internal/sem` indexer | fact **locus / file-anchor** extraction |\n| what | wall-clock ceiling so a hostile repo can't pin the indexer (DoS) | a regex that shreds hyphenated paths |\n\nOnly thing they share is that a security/review loop surfaced both. Different repos, different code, no causal link. Answer him separately.\n\n## 2. Your message\n\n```\nlast week:\n\nfinished the P0 Local Brain fix loop — every open brain PR reviewed, every trail\nfinding resolved and re-verified by weakening the guard\nlanded the entire-graph launch stack on main (39 trails) after the review pass\nsetup/doctor/status output rebuilt: short-form by default, and every printed\nremedy is now something the reader can actually run\ntwo security assessments closed (fast-xml-parser CVE, node-llama-cpp criticals)\n\nentire-brain\n• :review: Doctor warns when the install sits in a directory the OS may delete — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/315\n• :review: Setup output short-form by default, phase view behind --verbose — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/314\n• :review: Six compatibility aliases hidden from the advertised MCP surface — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/313\n• :review: A recorded component failure ages out once it rebuilds — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/312\n• :review: A writer refusing an unknown field is not corruption — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/311\n• :review: brain_recall over MCP, plus a guard against losing a tool again — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/310\n• :review: Pre-push gate settled, two env-only failures named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/309\n• :review: Semantic provider schema 1.3 ingested in full — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/308\n• :review: Seven-phase setup UI, capability block, distill consent — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/287\n• :review: A repo with no captured sessions is no longer reported broken — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/286\n• :review: Provider failure summarised instead of dumping the host CLI's help — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/285\n• :review: Test suite gets a deadline above its own runtime — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/267\n• :review: Ollama envelope guard bound by the client, not the writer — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/266\n• :review: Changelog since 0.1.0 and the integration branch for the fix stack — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/265\n• :review: Three remedies the reader could not follow — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/264\n• :review: Remedies rendered in the reader's own dispatch spelling — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/263\n• :review: Printed advice made runnable, escape hatch named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/262\n• :review: Our own installers stop blocking our own install — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/261\n• :review: Setup and status say what is true on a first run — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/260\n• :review: Bundle says what sharing a brain costs, at the moment it costs it — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/259\n• :review: Memory prepass says why it failed, stops retrying what cannot change — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/258\n• :review: Setup makes the brain discoverable and remembers what was declined — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/257\n• :review: Doctor prints only what a reader can act on — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/256\n• :review: Connect fails loudly when the hosted binding cannot be resolved — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/255\n• :review: Retrieval returns output an agent can accept, and discloses what was dropped — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/242\n• :review: Distill timeout configurable, nested-repo trap named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/241\n• :merged: Brain stops colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, ignoring local models — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/246\n\nentire-graph\n• :merged: Graph launch stack landed on current main — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/262\n• :merged: Committed-tree caches reused across queries, worktrees and clones — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/243\n• :merged: Go router group prefix fixed point bounded (hang on labstack/echo) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/226\n• :merged: Declaration-aware output and Go route analysis — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/236\n• :merged: Exact corpus-wide IDF statistics — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/214\n• :merged: Agent output no longer depends on measured latency — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/222\n• :merged: Multi-pattern git grep hang fixed, git children killed on signal — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/220\n• :merged: Every relation labelled EXTRACTED, INFERRED or AMBIGUOUS — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/195\n• :merged: Savings unfloored, only pipeline heads classified, writes detected — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/200\n• :merged: Guide asks for --format agent, ~2.9x cheaper per query — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/197\n• :merged: Opt-in prompt-time graph context hook for Claude Code — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/240\n• :merged: Untracked nested worktrees excluded from the corpus — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/203\n```\n\nTwo notes on it: entire-graph was 39 merged trails last week, I listed the headline plus 11 — say the word and I'll paste the full set. And cli #2292 (`investigate`/`review` error hints) has **no trail**, so I left it out rather than link a PR.\n\nNow the fix."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LSEo1oHYsSHbnMSZPpdB4y","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && git log --oneline -1 && sed -n '205,215p' internal/cli/facts_locus.go","description":"Confirm fresh worktree state"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"eaa97cc78aefcc8f3f29fba39a1a6c8336db6d1224845255c47b23ded9134a46","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LSEo1oHYsSHbnMSZPpdB4y","type":"tool_result","content":"0f23cbc2 Merge pull request #394 from entireio/soph/switch-to-refs\n\treturn out\n}\n\n// locusIdentifierPattern matches code-identifier-like tokens: backtick spans are\n// handled separately; this catches dotted paths (settings.Load), file paths\n// (internal/cli/facts.go), CamelCase, and snake_case identifiers.\nvar locusIdentifierPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:[./][A-Za-z0-9_]+)+|[A-Za-z_]*[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*|[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*_[A-Za-z0-9_]+`)\n\n// factLocus extracts the set of code identifiers a fact is about — the symbols,\n// packages, file paths, and refs named in its text (including backtick-quoted\n// spans). Returned lowercased and deduped. This is the locus signal: it lets","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"6b603a32ceac3a6bc7d456d464b12590f28705b88ce67de2b2f189d4d5eeff4e","message":{"role":"system","content":"# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors (was /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli)\n - This is a git worktree — an isolated copy of the repository. Run all commands from this directory. Do NOT `cd` to the original repository root.\n - The git stash stack is shared with the main checkout and all other worktrees, and other Claude sessions may push or pop it concurrently. Never use bare `git stash` / `git stash pop` — you could pop another session's changes. Prefer a temporary WIP commit to set work aside; if you must stash, use `git stash push -u -m \"<unique-tag>\"`, immediately capture your entry's SHA via `git stash list --format='%H %gs'`, restore with `git stash apply <sha>` (not pop), and afterwards drop the entry, re-finding its current `stash@{n}` by tag first.\n\n<total_tokens>14851900 tokens left</total_tokens>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"be1b65fb77a2584b0347e0f3774bcf0472cd9a7443de9482a2c8914935dc585d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the fix. First the failing test, against unpatched code:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GJKGMp47ug2gLAP46mjDrA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && cat >> internal/cli/facts_locus_test.go <<'EOF'\n\n// TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths pins the bug ashtom reported: the\n// extractor used to cut a hyphenated path into fragments, so a fact about\n// `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` was anchored to \"website/scripts/pre\" and\n// \"build.ts\" — two tokens that name nothing in the repo — while the real path\n// never appeared at all. Quoting the path in backticks did not help: the\n// backtick span added the correct token, but the regex sweep still produced\n// the fragments beside it, which is exactly what he saw.\nfunc TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths(t *testing.T) {\n\tcases := []struct {\n\t\tname string\n\t\ttext string\n\t\twant string\n\t}{\n\t\t{\"bare\", \"the website/scripts/pre-build.ts hook runs first\", \"website/scripts/pre-build.ts\"},\n\t\t{\"backticked\", \"see `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` for the hook\", \"website/scripts/pre-build.ts\"},\n\t\t{\"no directory\", \"pre-build.ts runs before the bundle step\", \"pre-build.ts\"},\n\t\t{\"hyphenated directory\", \"entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go owns this\", \"entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go\"},\n\t\t{\"leading dot\", \"edit .github/workflows/ci-windows.yml to add the shard\", \".github/workflows/ci-windows.yml\"},\n\t\t{\"dotted repo config\", \"the flag lives in .entire/settings.json\", \".entire/settings.json\"},\n\t}\n\tfor _, c := range cases {\n\t\tt.Run(c.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tgot := factLocus(c.text)\n\t\t\tloc := map[string]bool{}\n\t\t\tfor _, l := range got {\n\t\t\t\tloc[l] = true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif !loc[c.want] {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected locus token %q in %v\", c.want, got)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t// The fragments are the defect, not merely a missing token: a\n\t\t\t// fragment is a plausible-looking path that resolves to nothing,\n\t\t\t// which is worse than no anchor at all.\n\t\t\tfor _, frag := range []string{\"website/scripts/pre\", \"build.ts\", \"brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go\", \"github/workflows/ci\", \"windows.yml\", \"entire/settings.json\"} {\n\t\t\t\tif frag == c.want {\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif loc[frag] {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"fragment %q leaked into locus %v\", frag, got)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestFactLocusHyphenWideningStaysOffProse guards the other side of the fix:\n// admitting \"-\" must not turn ordinary hyphenated English into code anchors.\n// A segment separator (. or /) is still required, so prose stays empty.\nfunc TestFactLocusHyphenWideningStaysOffProse(t *testing.T) {\n\tfor _, text := range []string{\n\t\t\"a state-of-the-art approach with no code named in it\",\n\t\t\"we did a before-and-after comparison last week\",\n\t\t\"This sentence has only ordinary words in it.\",\n\t} {\n\t\tif got := factLocus(text); len(got) != 0 {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"prose %q should yield no locus, got %v\", text, got)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestLocusTokenIsFilePathSeesHyphenatedPaths closes the loop on drift: the\n// fragments were invisible to factLocusDrift (\"website/scripts/pre\" has no\n// extension, \"build.ts\" has no slash), so a hyphenated file could never be\n// reported as drifted no matter how long ago it was deleted.\nfunc TestLocusTokenIsFilePathSeesHyphenatedPaths(t *testing.T) {\n\tif !locusTokenIsFilePath(\"website/scripts/pre-build.ts\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"a hyphenated path with a real extension must count as a file path\")\n\t}\n\tif locusTokenIsFilePath(\"website/scripts/pre\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"an extensionless fragment must not count as a file path\")\n\t}\n}\nEOF\nenv -u FORCE_COLOR go test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestFactLocus|TestLocusToken' -count=1 2>&1 | tail -30","description":"Run new tests against unpatched code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"8cc64084e4d6191576bc407f5040866c83bcd582b8db370689e06dd5d311ab5b","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJKGMp47ug2gLAP46mjDrA","type":"tool_result","content":"--- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths/bare (0.00s)\n        facts_locus_test.go:288: expected locus token \"website/scripts/pre-build.ts\" in [build.ts website/scripts/pre]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"website/scripts/pre\" leaked into locus [build.ts website/scripts/pre]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"build.ts\" leaked into locus [build.ts website/scripts/pre]\n    --- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths/backticked (0.00s)\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"website/scripts/pre\" leaked into locus [build.ts website/scripts/pre website/scripts/pre-build.ts]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"build.ts\" leaked into locus [build.ts website/scripts/pre website/scripts/pre-build.ts]\n    --- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths/no_directory (0.00s)\n        facts_locus_test.go:288: expected locus token \"pre-build.ts\" in [build.ts]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"build.ts\" leaked into locus [build.ts]\n    --- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths/hyphenated_directory (0.00s)\n        facts_locus_test.go:288: expected locus token \"entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go\" in [brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go\" leaked into locus [brain/internal/cli/facts_locus.go]\n    --- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths/leading_dot (0.00s)\n        facts_locus_test.go:288: expected locus token \".github/workflows/ci-windows.yml\" in [github/workflows/ci windows.yml]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"github/workflows/ci\" leaked into locus [github/workflows/ci windows.yml]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"windows.yml\" leaked into locus [github/workflows/ci windows.yml]\n    --- FAIL: TestFactLocusKeepsHyphenatedPaths/dotted_repo_config (0.00s)\n        facts_locus_test.go:288: expected locus token \".entire/settings.json\" in [entire/settings.json]\n        facts_locus_test.go:298: fragment \"entire/settings.json\" leaked into locus [entire/settings.json]\nFAIL\nFAIL\tgithub.com/entireio/entire-brain/internal/cli\t0.995s\nFAIL","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"5aa1a10aa8d5d9d8d93736f8526d6e5b48fc94fd7d5cafa261bdf8e7c349b077","message":{"role":"system","content":"<total_tokens>14849655 tokens left</total_tokens>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"a6b5160be5152b837fb044c14e9cb69df4ea1f27c312d2115f5f7bf5340b5940","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Reproduced exactly — including ashtom's \"fragments still appear next to the correct paths\" in the backticked case. Now the fix:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016fJ8bLQ5xgokBokVYDnYoo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"internal/cli/facts_locus.go\")\ns = p.read_text()\n\nold_re = '''// locusIdentifierPattern matches code-identifier-like tokens: backtick spans are\n// handled separately; this catches dotted paths (settings.Load), file paths\n// (internal/cli/facts.go), CamelCase, and snake_case identifiers.\nvar locusIdentifierPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:[./][A-Za-z0-9_]+)+|[A-Za-z_]*[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*|[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*_[A-Za-z0-9_]+`)'''\n\nnew_re = '''// locusIdentifierPattern matches code-identifier-like tokens: backtick spans are\n// handled separately; this catches dotted paths (settings.Load), file paths\n// (internal/cli/facts.go), CamelCase, and snake_case identifiers.\n//\n// A path segment is `[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*` — interior hyphens are\n// part of the name. Without that, `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` was cut at the\n// hyphen and emitted as TWO tokens, \"website/scripts/pre\" and \"build.ts\",\n// neither of which names anything in the repo. That is worse than emitting\n// nothing: a fragment looks like a path, so it anchors a fact to a file that\n// does not exist, and locusTokenIsFilePath cannot even flag the drift (the\n// first fragment has no extension, the second has no slash). Hyphenated names\n// are not exotic here — .github/workflows/*, pre-build.ts, 20260320-no-raft.md.\n//\n// The hyphen must be INTERIOR (followed by more name), so a trailing dash is\n// left out of the token, and a separator (. or /) is still required for the\n// first alternative to fire at all — which is what keeps ordinary hyphenated\n// English (\"state-of-the-art\") out of the locus.\n//\n// The leading `\\\\.?` is the same defect for dot-directories: \".github/...\" was\n// emitted as \"github/...\", a path that resolves nowhere and would be reported\n// as drifted on every recall.\nvar locusIdentifierPattern = regexp.MustCompile(`\\\\.?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*(?:[./][A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*)+|[A-Za-z_]*[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*|[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*_[A-Za-z0-9_]+`)'''\n\nassert old_re in s\ns = s.replace(old_re, new_re, 1)\n\nold_add = '''\tset := map[string]struct{}{}\n\tadd := func(tok string) {\n\t\ttok = strings.ToLower(strings.Trim(tok, \"`.,;:()[]{}'\\\\\"\"))\n\t\tif len(tok) >= 3 {\n\t\t\tset[tok] = struct{}{}\n\t\t}\n\t}'''\n\nnew_add = '''\tset := map[string]struct{}{}\n\tadd := func(tok string) {\n\t\t// Trimmed asymmetrically: a LEADING dot is part of the name\n\t\t// (\".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \".entire/settings.json\"), a trailing one\n\t\t// is sentence punctuation. Trimming both ends, as this did, silently\n\t\t// renamed every dot-directory path in the corpus.\n\t\ttok = strings.ToLower(strings.TrimRight(strings.TrimLeft(tok, locusLeadingTrimCutset), locusTrailingTrimCutset))\n\t\tif len(tok) >= 3 {\n\t\t\tset[tok] = struct{}{}\n\t\t}\n\t}'''\n\nassert old_add in s\ns = s.replace(old_add, new_add, 1)\n\nold_bt = 'var backtickSpanPattern = regexp.MustCompile(\"`([^`]+)`\")'\nnew_bt = '''const (\n\t// locusLeadingTrimCutset omits \".\" on purpose; see add in factLocus.\n\tlocusLeadingTrimCutset  = \"`,;:([{'\\\\\"\"\n\tlocusTrailingTrimCutset = \"`.,;:)]}'\\\\\"\"\n)\n\nvar backtickSpanPattern = regexp.MustCompile(\"`([^`]+)`\")'''\nassert old_bt in s\ns = s.replace(old_bt, new_bt, 1)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPY\ngofmt -l internal/cli/facts_locus.go; env -u FORCE_COLOR go test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestFactLocus|TestLocusToken|TestLocusOverlap' -count=1 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Apply locus fix and re-run tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
