{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"b072b1daf7e7fd7e42c8c39c83601c65dd89f4838cf3d99b84db968e3c671bb1","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012ahrstBtqqsnF4AgvZ1PPg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(facts): stop the locus extractor cutting paths at hyphens and dots\n\nA fact about `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` was anchored to two tokens that\nname nothing: \"website/scripts/pre\" and \"build.ts\". The path itself never\nappeared. Quoting it in backticks did not help — the backtick span added the\ncorrect token, but the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it,\nwhich is what the reporter saw after re-recording the fact.\n\nTwo separate cuts in locusIdentifierPattern, same class:\n\n  - No \"-\" in any segment class, so a segment ended at the first hyphen and\n    the remainder restarted as a new token. .github/workflows/*, pre-build.ts\n    and 20260320-no-raft.md are not exotic names here.\n  - No leading \".\", and add() trimmed the cutset from BOTH ends, so\n    \".github/workflows/ci.yml\" was recorded as \"github/workflows/ci.yml\".\n\nA fragment is worse than a missing anchor. It looks like a path, so it binds\nthe fact to a file that does not exist, and factLocusDrift cannot flag it:\n\"website/scripts/pre\" has no extension and \"build.ts\" has no slash, so neither\nreaches the stat. A hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it\nwould ever be reported as drifted.\n\nSegments are now `[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*`: the hyphen must be\ninterior, so a trailing dash stays out of the token, and the first alternative\nstill requires a \".\" or \"/\", which is what keeps ordinary hyphenated English\n(\"state-of-the-art\") out of the locus. add() trims leading and trailing\npunctuation separately, keeping a leading dot.\n\nStored facts self-heal: `reclassify` already rewrites Locus when it differs\nfrom what the text derives, so the fragments go away on the next pass without\na migration.\n\nVerified by weakening: dropping the hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the\nasymmetric trim each turns the new tests red; all three restored, green.\nFull internal/cli suite green (211s).\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
