{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"18812e30aeb0c63ea69a4cb69fece85c70cd6b64e9eb77cdc3e8b5318de7af43","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BHNAaissTUySGTLbmakzXx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base main --head fix/locus-hyphenated-paths --title \"fix(facts): stop the locus extractor cutting paths at hyphens and dots\" --body-file - <<'BODY' 2>&1 | tail -3\nReported by @ashtom: a fact about `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` was anchored to `website/scripts/pre` and `build.ts` — two tokens that name nothing in the repo — while the real path never appeared. Re-recording the fact with the path in backticks did not help: the backtick span added the correct token, but the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it.\n\n## Root cause\n\nOne regex, `locusIdentifierPattern` in `internal/cli/facts_locus.go`. Two cuts of the same class:\n\n1. **No `-` in any segment class.** A segment ended at the first hyphen and the remainder restarted as a fresh token. `.github/workflows/*`, `pre-build.ts`, `20260320-no-raft.md` are routine names here.\n2. **No leading `.`**, and `add()` trimmed its cutset from *both* ends, so `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was stored as `github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n\n## Why a fragment is worse than no anchor\n\nIt looks like a path, so it binds the fact to a file that does not exist — and `factLocusDrift` can't flag it. `locusTokenIsFilePath` needs a slash *and* an extension: `website/scripts/pre` has no extension, `build.ts` has no slash. Neither reaches the `os.Stat`. **A hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it would ever be reported as drifted.** The leading-dot case is the opposite failure: `github/workflows/ci.yml` *does* pass the file-path test and resolves nowhere, so it is reported as drifted on every recall, forever.\n\n## The fix\n\nSegments become `[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*`, and an optional leading `.` is admitted. The hyphen must be **interior**, so a trailing dash stays out of the token, and the first alternative still requires a `.` or `/` — which is what keeps ordinary hyphenated English out of the locus. `add()` now trims leading and trailing punctuation with separate cutsets.\n\n```\n                                before                              after\nwebsite/scripts/pre-build.ts    [website/scripts/pre, build.ts]     [website/scripts/pre-build.ts]\nentire-brain/internal/x.go      [brain/internal/x.go]               [entire-brain/internal/x.go]\n.github/workflows/ci-win.yml    [github/workflows/ci, win.yml]      [.github/workflows/ci-win.yml]\nstate-of-the-art prose          []                                  []\n```\n\n## Migration\n\nNone needed. `reclassify` already rewrites `Locus` when it differs from what the text derives (`facts_locus.go:158`), so stored facts shed their fragments on the next pass.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The new tests fail on `main` with exactly the reported symptom, including the backticked case.\n- **Verified by weakening**: dropping the interior-hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the asymmetric trim each turns them red. All three restored → green.\n- `TestFactLocusHyphenWideningStaysOffProse` guards the other side: admitting `-` must not turn hyphenated English into code anchors.\n- `locusTokenIsFilePath` test closes the drift loop.\n- Full `internal/cli` suite green (211s), `go build ./...` and `go vet` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY","description":"Open the PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
