{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"be83948572c8a38b212f6521147f39f2633b85556bdee05fa42257b4f9a003f4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cf8w2RjKx2oXpztDpA5HmG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-create-rejects-pr-branch.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: trail-create-rejects-pr-branch\ndescription: entire trail create 422s on a branch that already has an open PR; branchless create works, so create the trail BEFORE the PR\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`entire trail create --branch <b>` returns a bare `validation_error` 422 (no field\ndetail) when `<b>` already has an open GitHub PR. `PATCH .../trails/<n>` with\n`{\"branchName\":..., \"branchAction\":\"link\"}` is refused the same way, so you cannot\nattach a branch to an existing trail after the fact either. A **branchless** create\n(POST with title/body and no branchName) returns 201, which is how you isolate it —\nthe endpoint and auth are fine, only the branch link is rejected.\n\nConfirmed 2026-10-19 on entireio/entire-brain: PR #410 was opened with `gh pr create`\nfirst, and every subsequent attempt to give it a trail 422'd. Probe trail #323 proved\nthe endpoint healthy; it cannot be deleted either (\"Owned Changes cannot be deleted\nthrough the repository Trail API\") — close it with `status: \"closed\"` instead.\n\n**Why:** this contradicts [[pr-author-not-entire-app]], which says to run `gh pr create`\nbefore `entire trail create` so the PR author is you and not the bot. Both cannot hold:\nPR-first gets you the right author and NO trail; trail-first gets you a trail and a\nbot-authored PR. There is no ordering that gives both today.\n\n**How to apply:** decide which you need before pushing. If the work must appear in a\ntrail-linked status report, run `entire trail create` first and accept the bot author.\nIf authorship matters more, open the PR with `gh` and accept that it has no trail — do\nnot close and reopen the PR to retrofit one without asking, it churns the PR number and\nthe author. Diagnose any trail 422 by retrying the same POST without `branchName`.\nEOF\nprintf '%s\\n' '- [Trail create rejects a PR branch](trail-create-rejects-pr-branch.md) — 422 with no detail when the branch already has an open PR; branchless create 201s; conflicts with pr-author-not-entire-app' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\ntail -2 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Record the trail-create gotcha"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QBEdj5ivddWeGiEvwvi8DU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && entire brain remember \"entire-brain's fact locus extractor (locusIdentifierPattern, internal/cli/facts_locus.go) cut file paths at hyphens and dropped leading dots: a fact about \\`website/scripts/pre-build.ts\\` was anchored to \\`website/scripts/pre\\` and \\`build.ts\\`, and \\`.github/workflows/ci.yml\\` was stored as \\`github/workflows/ci.yml\\`. A fragment is worse than a missing anchor because it looks like a path but resolves nowhere, and factLocusDrift cannot flag it (locusTokenIsFilePath needs both a slash and an extension). Fixed in PR #410 by making a path segment [A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)* with an optional leading dot, and by trimming punctuation asymmetrically in factLocus's add(). Reported by ashtom.\" --path architecture.retrieval.gotcha --json 2>&1 | tail -6","description":"Record the durable brain fact"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
