{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"8549dbe47cd523c4a1bdacd515bd9ded75eb484d8f5e48a74f3f3a6a6beca995","message":{"role":"system","content":"<total_tokens>14816286 tokens left</total_tokens>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"d0dca2bb886f4f91dbac45eac07834a216fa2850205ad3991913ee9439fca8a4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Done. All CI green on the fix.\n\n## The bug — found, fixed, PR #410\n\nashtom was right, and it's one regex: `locusIdentifierPattern` in `internal/cli/facts_locus.go:211`. **No `-` in any path-segment class**, so a segment ended at the first hyphen and the remainder restarted as a new token.\n\n```\nwebsite/scripts/pre-build.ts  →  [\"website/scripts/pre\", \"build.ts\"]\n```\n\nExactly what he saw. Backticks didn't help because the backtick span added the correct token while the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it.\n\nSame function had a second cut of the same class: no leading `.`, and `add()` trimmed its punctuation cutset from **both** ends — so `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was stored as `github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n\n**Why a fragment is worse than no anchor.** It looks like a path, so it binds the fact to a file that doesn't exist — and `factLocusDrift` can't catch it. `locusTokenIsFilePath` needs a slash *and* an extension: `website/scripts/pre` has no extension, `build.ts` has no slash. Neither reaches the `os.Stat`. A hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it would ever be flagged as drifted. The dot case fails the other way: `github/workflows/ci.yml` *does* pass the file-path test and resolves nowhere, so it reads as drifted forever.\n\nSegments are now `[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*` with an optional leading dot. The hyphen must be interior (trailing dash stays out) and a `.` or `/` is still required, which keeps `state-of-the-art` prose out of the locus.\n\n- Tests fail on main with the exact reported symptom, backticked case included\n- **Verified by weakening**: dropping the hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the asymmetric trim each goes red; all three restored → green\n- Full `internal/cli` green (211s), build + vet clean, CI **29 pass / 1 skip**\n- No migration: `reclassify` already rewrites `Locus` when it differs from the text, so stored facts shed fragments on the next pass\n\nLive proof it's real — I recorded a fact about this with your currently-installed brain, and its locus came back:\n```\n['build.ts', ..., 'github/workflows/ci.yml', ..., 'website/scripts/pre', 'website/scripts/pre-build.ts']\n```\n\n## One thing I couldn't do: give #410 a trail\n\n`entire trail create --branch fix/locus-hyphenated-paths` → `422 validation_error`, no field detail. Same for `PATCH` with `branchAction: \"link\"`. A **branchless** create returns 201, so the endpoint and auth are fine — it's the branch link that's refused, because the branch already has an open PR.\n\nThat collides with your existing rule (`gh pr create` before `entire trail create`, else the PR author is the bot). PR-first → right author, no trail. Trail-first → trail, bot-authored PR. No ordering gives both right now.\n\nI left #410 as-is rather than close and reopen it to retrofit a trail — that churns the number and the author, and it's your call. Say the word and I'll redo it trail-first. (Probe trail #323 is closed; it can't be deleted — \"Owned Changes cannot be deleted through the repository Trail API\".)\n\nUnchanged and still yours: approve/merge **#395 before #329**, close **#340**."}]}}
