{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"f015fce50ae48cd81d0eea961bff6d2112ea783f0bdd2f8174580315b73c2d75","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163sKuMoX4pQoYWwCQizZCk","type":"tool_result","content":"HTTP/2.0 201 Created\nVary: Accept-Encoding\nX-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\n\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io/api/v1/schemas/TrailCreateResponseBody.json\",\n  \"trail\": {\n    \"id\": \"01M5A6DR7SXGE6BXH8EEXV9YD0\",\n    \"number\": 324,\n    \"url\": \"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/324\",\n    \"title\": \"fix(facts): stop the locus extractor cutting paths at hyphens and dots\",\n    \"status\": \"open\",\n    \"branch\": \"fix/locus-hyphenated-paths\",\n    \"original_branch\": \"fix/locus-hyphenated-paths\",\n    \"base\": \"main\",\n    \"type\": \"task\",\n    \"priority\": \"none\",\n    \"author\": {\n      \"id\": \"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771\",\n      \"login\": \"suhaanthayyil\",","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"3ed04d1d60af10d1a18394fdac69bea2a548e6172f9510f5627bb36ad89ec3e0","message":{"role":"system","content":"<total_tokens>14798606 tokens left</total_tokens>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"e0479125f094aa43aab76a324329681603f332e0a3b5d2898698ceb5c12e1967","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Trail **#324**, linked to the branch, authored as you, PR #410 untouched. My earlier read was wrong — it was never the PR, it was the stale CLI sending camelCase. Adding the body:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PT5NuJ7h1UuFwZ9J6o2Qbp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nbody='''Reported by @ashtom: a fact about \\`website/scripts/pre-build.ts\\` was anchored to \\`website/scripts/pre\\` and \\`build.ts\\` — two tokens that name nothing in the repo — while the real path never appeared. Re-recording it with the path in backticks did not help: the backtick span added the correct token, but the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it.\n\n## Root cause\n\nOne regex, \\`locusIdentifierPattern\\` in \\`internal/cli/facts_locus.go\\`. Two cuts of the same class:\n\n1. **No \\`-\\` in any segment class.** A segment ended at the first hyphen and the remainder restarted as a fresh token.\n2. **No leading \\`.\\`**, and \\`add()\\` trimmed its cutset from *both* ends, so \\`.github/workflows/ci.yml\\` was stored as \\`github/workflows/ci.yml\\`.\n\n## Why a fragment is worse than no anchor\n\nIt looks like a path, so it binds the fact to a file that does not exist — and \\`factLocusDrift\\` cannot catch it. \\`locusTokenIsFilePath\\` needs a slash *and* an extension: \\`website/scripts/pre\\` has no extension, \\`build.ts\\` has no slash. A hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it would ever be flagged as drifted. The leading-dot case fails the other way: \\`github/workflows/ci.yml\\` does pass the file-path test and resolves nowhere, so it reads as drifted forever.\n\n## The fix\n\nSegments become \\`[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*\\` with an optional leading dot. The hyphen must be **interior**, and the first alternative still requires a \\`.\\` or \\`/\\` — which keeps ordinary hyphenated English out of the locus. \\`add()\\` trims leading and trailing punctuation with separate cutsets.\n\nNo migration: \\`reclassify\\` already rewrites \\`Locus\\` when it differs from what the text derives, so stored facts shed their fragments on the next pass.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The new tests fail on main with exactly the reported symptom, backticked case included.\n- **Verified by weakening**: dropping the interior-hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the asymmetric trim each turns them red. All three restored, green.\n- Full \\`internal/cli\\` suite green (211s); build and vet clean; 29 CI checks pass.\n\nGitHub PR: https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/410'''\nprint(json.dumps({'body':body,'type':'bug'}))\n\" | entire api --to cell -X PATCH -i --input - \"/api/v1/trails/gh/entireio/entire-brain/324\" 2>&1 | sed -n '1p'","description":"Attach the full body to trail 324"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
