{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"bda2b21804901ef01cc43ee938e4e3fe7e2986557ebcb13e5f4d6d71682b089a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H2WRVkaDj8j3SdHT3qN8FS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nbody='''Reported by @ashtom: a fact about \\`website/scripts/pre-build.ts\\` was anchored to \\`website/scripts/pre\\` and \\`build.ts\\` — two tokens that name nothing in the repo — while the real path never appeared. Re-recording it with the path in backticks did not help: the backtick span added the correct token, but the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it.\n\n## Root cause\n\nOne regex, \\`locusIdentifierPattern\\` in \\`internal/cli/facts_locus.go\\`. Two cuts of the same class:\n\n1. **No \\`-\\` in any segment class.** A segment ended at the first hyphen and the remainder restarted as a fresh token.\n2. **No leading \\`.\\`**, and \\`add()\\` trimmed its cutset from *both* ends, so \\`.github/workflows/ci.yml\\` was stored as \\`github/workflows/ci.yml\\`.\n\n## Why a fragment is worse than no anchor\n\nIt looks like a path, so it binds the fact to a file that does not exist — and \\`factLocusDrift\\` cannot catch it. \\`locusTokenIsFilePath\\` needs a slash *and* an extension: \\`website/scripts/pre\\` has no extension, \\`build.ts\\` has no slash. Neither reaches the stat, so a hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it would ever be flagged as drifted. The leading-dot case fails the other way: \\`github/workflows/ci.yml\\` does pass the file-path test and resolves nowhere, so it reads as drifted forever.\n\n## The fix\n\nSegments become \\`[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*\\` with an optional leading dot. The hyphen must be **interior**, so a trailing dash stays out of the token, and the first alternative still requires a \\`.\\` or \\`/\\` — which is what keeps ordinary hyphenated English out of the locus. \\`add()\\` trims leading and trailing punctuation with separate cutsets.\n\nNo migration: \\`reclassify\\` already rewrites \\`Locus\\` when it differs from what the text derives, so stored facts shed their fragments on the next pass.\n\n## Verification\n\n- The new tests fail on main with exactly the reported symptom, backticked case included.\n- **Verified by weakening**: dropping the interior-hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the asymmetric trim each turns them red. All three restored, green.\n- Full \\`internal/cli\\` suite green (211s); build and vet clean; 29 CI checks pass, 1 skipped.\n\nGitHub PR: https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/410'''\nprint(json.dumps({'markdown':body,'overwrite':True}))\n\" | entire api --to cell -X PUT -i --input - \"/api/v1/trails/gh/entireio/entire-brain/324/body\" 2>&1 | sed -n '1p'; echo \"--- set type\"; echo '{\"type\":\"bug\"}' | entire api --to cell -X PATCH -i --input - \"/api/v1/trails/gh/entireio/entire-brain/324\" 2>&1 | sed -n '1p'","description":"Write the trail body and set type"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
