{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"ad297bcbf10eac4491fe08c3ea83b4b66f2f3e0b8913ede1723741c3bac7aa03","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now correcting the memory note — my first diagnosis was wrong:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WQgaUEDHtRBsXnmGWg1Edz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-create-rejects-pr-branch.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: trail-create-rejects-pr-branch\ndescription: entire trail create 422s because the installed CLI sends camelCase; the cell wants snake_case branch_name/branch_action with additionalProperties false\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`entire trail create --branch <b>` returns a bare `validation_error` 422 with no\nfield detail. It is **not** the branch, the PR, or the server. The cell's\n`TrailCreateRequestJSON` declares `branch_name` and `branch_action` in\n**snake_case** with `additionalProperties: false`, and the installed CLI posts\n`branchName`/`branchAction`, so every field is an unknown property and the whole\nbody is rejected.\n\nPost it yourself and it works, with you as the author and the existing PR untouched:\n\n    echo '{\"title\":\"...\",\"branch_name\":\"<b>\",\"branch_action\":\"link\"}' \\\n      | entire api --to cell -X POST --input - \"/api/v1/trails/gh/<owner>/<repo>\"\n\nThe description is a separate document — `TrailUpdateRequestJSON` has no `body`\nfield, so a PATCH carrying one 400s. Write it to\n`PUT /api/v1/trails/gh/<owner>/<repo>/<n>/body` as `{\"markdown\":..., \"overwrite\":true}`.\nGates live only on the repo-id route: `/api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/trails/<n>/gates`\n(the host-addressed path 404s), and `entire api` fills `{repo_id}` from origin.\n\n**Why:** this is the same class as [[stale-entire-binary-finding-404]] — payloads\nmoved to snake_case and an old local binary still speaks the old shape, failing with\na status code that blames your request. I first concluded the open PR was blocking\nthe branch link, which was wrong; a branchless create returning 201 was consistent\nwith that theory too, so it did not falsify anything. Reading the OpenAPI schema did.\n\n**How to apply:** on any `entire` 422 with no field detail, fetch\n`entire api --to cell /api/v1/openapi.yaml` and diff the request schema against what\nthe CLI sends before theorising about server state. Do NOT close and reopen a PR to\nretrofit a trail — linking a branch that already has a PR works fine. This supersedes\nthe ordering worry in [[pr-author-not-entire-app]]: PR-first keeps your authorship\nAND can still get a trail.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold = \"- [Trail create rejects a PR branch](trail-create-rejects-pr-branch.md) — 422 with no detail when the branch already has an open PR; branchless create 201s; conflicts with pr-author-not-entire-app\"\nnew = \"- [Trail create 422 is a stale CLI](trail-create-rejects-pr-branch.md) — cell wants snake_case branch_name/branch_action + additionalProperties:false; read the OpenAPI before blaming server state\"\nassert old in s\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1))\nprint(\"index corrected\")\nPY","description":"Correct the memory note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
