{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"f93724ceab8eff040b4dd7ca2bbefd2bb3a4c14bf586831dbae2956545ad9d42","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PATau6vo2TrFpFeNAi7gkL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\":[{\"id\":\"COR-2175\",\"title\":\"Watch daemon blocks itself: the memory worker it launches holds write.lock, so that tick's refresh fails brain_locked and skips distill\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2175/watch-daemon-blocks-itself-the-memory-worker-it-launches-holds\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T06:42:35.075Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2055\",\"title\":\"Make Brain extraction incremental and cost-bounded\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2055/make-brain-extraction-incremental-and-cost-bounded\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T06:42:34.947Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2177\",\"title\":\"Distill re-spends on every branch copy of a session: merged sessions are distilled again from scratch on main\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2177/distill-re-spends-on-every-branch-copy-of-a-session-merged-sessions\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T06:42:33.776Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2174\",\"title\":\"Upgrading entire-brain silently wedges the watch daemon: every tick fails, distill never runs, status says ✓ running\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2174/upgrading-entire-brain-silently-wedges-the-watch-daemon-every-tick\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T05:06:45.006Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2176\",\"title\":\"watch.log has no timestamps and most lines don't say which repo or tick they belong to\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2176/watchlog-has-no-timestamps-and-most-lines-dont-say-which-repo-or-tick\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T05:06:44.738Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":3,\"name\":\"Medium\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2162\",\"title\":\"A component stays \\\"failed\\\" after the cause is gone, and two status surfaces disagree about it\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2162/a-component-stays-failed-after-the-cause-is-gone-and-two-status\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T04:56:25.208Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2154\",\"title\":\"Replace facts semantic retrieval (bundled embedder + RRF) with in-process BM25 + taxonomy filters\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2154/replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with-in-process\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T04:02:21.307Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2164\",\"title\":\"Assess inherited critical argv-parser advisory in benchmark Git tooling\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2164/assess-inherited-critical-argv-parser-advisory-in-benchmark-git\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T04:02:21.290Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2145\",\"title\":\"Assess setup-go v7 bundled XML-parser advisory and workflow exposure\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2145/assess-setup-go-v7-bundled-xml-parser-advisory-and-workflow-exposure\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T01:26:07.092Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2159\",\"title\":\"Prove the MCP surface works in both hosts, not just the one we develop in\",\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2159/prove-the-mcp-surface-works-in-both-hosts-not-just-the-one-we-develop\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T01:34:32.935Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2146\",\"title\":\"entire-graph: a promisor remote makes the semantic snapshot identity-less, and Brain correctly refuses it\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2146/entire-graph-a-promisor-remote-makes-the-semantic-snapshot-identity\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T01:34:15.915Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2158\",\"title\":\"Six of the 37 MCP tools are self-declared aliases; classify the surface and hide the duplicates\",\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2158/six-of-the-37-mcp-tools-are-self-declared-aliases-classify-the-surface\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T21:12:30.879Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2153\",\"title\":\"Retrieval returns output an agent can accept, and discloses what was dropped\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2153/retrieval-returns-output-an-agent-can-accept-and-discloses-what-was\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T20:45:15.188Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2163\",\"title\":\"brain_remember exists on main and is missing from the released binary; brain_recall does not exist at all\",\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2163/brain-remember-exists-on-main-and-is-missing-from-the-released-binary\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T20:27:33.342Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2007\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: read entire-graph semantic schema 1.3 (Brain still pins 1.1)\",\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2007/entire-brain-read-entire-graph-semantic-schema-13-brain-still-pins-11\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T20:26:59.667Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2059\",\"title\":\"Remove Brain’s duplicate transcript storage\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2059/remove-brains-duplicate-transcript-storage\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T23:25:50.348Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2054\",\"title\":\"Replace Brain’s polling watcher with an event-driven worker\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2054/replace-brains-polling-watcher-with-an-event-driven-worker\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T23:25:47.151Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2157\",\"title\":\"Cut a stable entire-brain release and re-run the outsider install against it\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2157/cut-a-stable-entire-brain-release-and-re-run-the-outsider-install\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:32:51.780Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2147\",\"title\":\"Generated agent guides must use commands the released Graph actually has\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2147/generated-agent-guides-must-use-commands-the-released-graph-actually\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:29:51.917Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2136\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: unblock nanoid security patch with isolated benchmark fixtures\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2136/entire-brain-unblock-nanoid-security-patch-with-isolated-benchmark\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.463Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2139\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: resolve go-git dependency-update merge conflicts\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2139/entire-brain-resolve-go-git-dependency-update-merge-conflicts\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.340Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2156\",\"title\":\"Brain's Git reads must not lock the user's shared index\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2156/brains-git-reads-must-not-lock-the-users-shared-index\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:01:26.977Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2150\",\"title\":\"Everything Brain prints must be something the reader can actually run\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2150/everything-brain-prints-must-be-something-the-reader-can-actually-run\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:57:04.977Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2160\",\"title\":\"CI has two required \\\"benchmark\\\" jobs and neither is a regression floor\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2160/ci-has-two-required-benchmark-jobs-and-neither-is-a-regression-floor\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:39:25.841Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2161\",\"title\":\"Land the BrainMark harness fixes before anything is gated on its scores\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2161/land-the-brainmark-harness-fixes-before-anything-is-gated-on-its\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:39:16.291Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2001\",\"title\":\"entire-brain CLI: hide developer-only commands, group operator commands in --help\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2001/entire-brain-cli-hide-developer-only-commands-group-operator-commands\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:38:26.949Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2006\",\"title\":\"Simplify Brain’s default setup and commands\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2006/simplify-brains-default-setup-and-commands\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:38:26.949Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2002\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: fix local dev loop (mise lint/test fail locally, internal/cli timeout) and settle pre-push guidance\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2002/entire-brain-fix-local-dev-loop-mise-linttest-fail-locally-internalcli\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:11:00.104Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2151\",\"title\":\"Entire's own files must not make Entire's own install gate refuse\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2151/entires-own-files-must-not-make-entires-own-install-gate-refuse\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:10:44.987Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2155\",\"title\":\"Sharing a brain must name what it costs, at the moment it costs it\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2155/sharing-a-brain-must-name-what-it-costs-at-the-moment-it-costs-it\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:10:44.987Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2152\",\"title\":\"A failed memory prepass must record why, and stop retrying what cannot change\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2152/a-failed-memory-prepass-must-record-why-and-stop-retrying-what-cannot\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:10:44.987Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2149\",\"title\":\"Setup wires the brain in, asks before spending tokens, and remembers a decline\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2149/setup-wires-the-brain-in-asks-before-spending-tokens-and-remembers-a\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:10:44.987Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2148\",\"title\":\"First run tells the truth: a healthy new repo must not report itself broken\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2148/first-run-tells-the-truth-a-healthy-new-repo-must-not-report-itself\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:10:44.987Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2138\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: resolve setup-go dependency-update merge conflicts\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2138/entire-brain-resolve-setup-go-dependency-update-merge-conflicts\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T00:32:21.859Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2144\",\"title\":\"Capture diagnostic context for intermittent Git fixture HEAD parse failures\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2144/capture-diagnostic-context-for-intermittent-git-fixture-head-parse\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T00:25:23.797Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":3,\"name\":\"Medium\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2137\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: resolve go-billy dependency-update merge conflicts\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2137/entire-brain-resolve-go-billy-dependency-update-merge-conflicts\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-15T23:15:09.721Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2129\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: establish a verified Go dependency security baseline\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2129/entire-brain-establish-a-verified-go-dependency-security-baseline\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-15T10:02:25.848Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2052\",\"title\":\"Remove Graph from Brain’s memory workflow\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2052/remove-graph-from-brains-memory-workflow\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-14T04:08:53.623Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2062\",\"title\":\"Retire unused Brain subsystems and dependencies\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2062/retire-unused-brain-subsystems-and-dependencies\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:43.432Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2061\",\"title\":\"Unify Brain local and hosted memory retrieval\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2061/unify-brain-local-and-hosted-memory-retrieval\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:42.679Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2060\",\"title\":\"Make Brain hosted publication revision-aware and retryable\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2060/make-brain-hosted-publication-revision-aware-and-retryable\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:40.249Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2058\",\"title\":\"Preserve Brain memory history and tighten supersession\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2058/preserve-brain-memory-history-and-tighten-supersession\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:36.137Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2057\",\"title\":\"Migrate Brain local memory storage to SQLite per repository\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2057/migrate-brain-local-memory-storage-to-sqlite-per-repository\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:35.405Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2056\",\"title\":\"Define Brain’s simplified memory and revision contract\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2056/define-brains-simplified-memory-and-revision-contract\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:34.607Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2053\",\"title\":\"Add nonblocking Entire lifecycle notifications for plugins\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2053/add-nonblocking-entire-lifecycle-notifications-for-plugins\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T03:59:31.802Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2005\",\"title\":\"entire-brain docs refresh\",\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2005/entire-brain-docs-refresh\",\"assignee\":null,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-08T18:15:27.441Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}},{\"id\":\"COR-2000\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: contributing docs with glossary and internal architecture overview\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2000/entire-brain-contributing-docs-with-glossary-and-internal-architecture\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-05T03:22:12.197Z\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"}}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MVmxqz2v7Lw1Fx2bfZnfda","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"P-COR-39\",\"uuid\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"icon\":\":seedling:\",\"color\":\"#bec2c8\",\"name\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"summary\":\"Code done + CI-gated (v0.1.0 tagged, 28/30 bench, beats CBM 1215-822). NOT finished: the repos are still private. P0 closes when the brain is released and installable.\",\"description\":\"**Finish and GA the local brain.** The local brain runs today, so P0 is release hygiene and version-stamping, not new build. The rest of the arc depends on a frozen contract.\\n\\nPieces that are live now:\\n\\n* **entire-sem**: the semantic provider (tree-sitter structural extraction, no vectors).\\n* **entire-brain**: durable, branch-scoped, provenance-anchored facts plus a local MCP surface of about 33 tools.\\n* **brain-bench**: a CI gate that benchmarks the extractor against a reference tool across roughly 30 languages and fails on regression or drift.\\n\\nGate: none. Everything ships already, but nothing is formally tagged.\",\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p0-ga-the-local-brain-9e185727dce2\",\"resourceCount\":0,\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-09T01:24:08.545Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-05T03:00:44.736Z\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-07-09T01:24:08.571Z\",\"completedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"startDate\":\"2026-07-01\",\"startDateResolution\":\"month\",\"targetDate\":\"2026-08-31\",\"targetDateResolution\":\"month\",\"priority\":{\"value\":1,\"name\":\"Urgent\"},\"labels\":[\"Semantic Layer Squad\"],\"initiatives\":[{\"id\":\"c1fba6dc-5025-43bd-9e9e-08792e1f7386\",\"name\":\"Semantic Reasoning Layer\"}],\"lead\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"leadTeam\":{\"id\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\",\"name\":\"Core\",\"key\":\"COR\"},\"status\":{\"id\":\"d8d63886-b7b9-4d7e-8c86-930109b86579\",\"name\":\"In Progress\",\"type\":\"started\"},\"teams\":[{\"id\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\",\"name\":\"Core\",\"key\":\"COR\"}],\"milestones\":[{\"id\":\"904b2ac6-145e-460c-9f6a-d6d799ca60a2\",\"name\":\"M1 Harden and GA entire-sem\",\"description\":\"Version-stamp entire-sem and freeze the schema so everything downstream can trust the contract.\",\"targetDate\":\"2026-07-31\",\"progress\":\"8%\"},{\"id\":\"bc05f7ea-a603-4d11-bcdc-d9ef4afb9d74\",\"name\":\"M2 Close the brain blockers\",\"description\":\"Ship the local brain with honest claims, no overreach.\",\"targetDate\":\"2026-08-15\",\"progress\":\"0%\"},{\"id\":\"d1e49492-c5ba-486a-b5df-8a8b17aad84d\",\"name\":\"M3 GA the MCP surface for both plugins\",\"description\":\"Harden the local MCP tool surface for the Claude Code and Codex plugins.\",\"targetDate\":\"2026-08-15\",\"progress\":\"25%\"},{\"id\":\"d7ffe1d3-5674-4a6d-bc9f-cb949cab4a0c\",\"name\":\"M4 brain-bench as the automated eval gate\",\"description\":\"Make brain-bench a required regression floor in CI.\",\"targetDate\":\"2026-08-31\",\"progress\":\"0%\"},{\"id\":\"b96f5a38-d131-40f1-bbeb-9e04f95c8f20\",\"name\":\"M5 Release + distribution\",\"description\":\"The actual finish line: make entire-brain + entire-sem available beyond the team, an install path, docs, and the announcement. P0 is done when someone outside the team can install and run it.\\n\\n**Status corrected 2026-10-16** (evidence in the project comment thread):\\n\\n* **Repos are PUBLIC.** `entireio/entire-brain` and `entireio/entire-graph` are both public — the old title said \\\"the brain is still private\\\", which is no longer true.\\n* **The install path works.** `curl -fsSL .../scripts/get-brain.sh | bash` run from a clean directory returns exit 0, verifies checksums, and produces a working binary.\\n* **What remains: a stable release.** entire-brain has shipped `v0.1.0` (2026-09-20) and nothing since; entire-graph is on v0.4.0. An outsider installing today gets a binary that is **356 commits / 46 merged PRs behind main**. The pipeline is healthy — nightlies publish daily.\\n\\nSo the exit criterion is met in mechanism but not in content: they can install, they just get a stale brain. Remaining: land the open fix PRs, cut a stable v0.2.0, then re-run the outsider install and confirm the new version.\\n\\n**Hazard:** tags `v0.2.0`, `v0.3.0`, `v0.3.1` exist as local-only tags and were never pushed. `release.yml` fires on `push: tags: v*`, so a stray `git push --tags` would publish from whatever they point at.\",\"targetDate\":\"2026-07-31\",\"progress\":\"50%\"},{\"id\":\"b3b9c5e4-e502-4b63-9f45-382109d35556\",\"name\":\"Post launch\",\"description\":null,\"targetDate\":null,\"progress\":\"35%\"}]}"}]}]}}
