{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"5fbe0f25f12c2f0fb3095d868d15af389a3763fe5914e6c90a41e101c8a2d94f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Status report — P0 · GA the Local Brain\n\n**Project:** [P0 · GA the Local Brain](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p0-ga-the-local-brain-9e185727dce2) (P-COR-39, Core, Urgent) · 48 issues · **9 Done**\n\n## PR state — 27 open, measured today\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| Mergeable, no conflicts | **27 / 27** |\n| GitHub Actions fully green | **27 / 27** |\n| `findings` gate passed (zero open review findings) | **27 / 27** |\n| `up_to_date` gate passed | **27 / 27** |\n| `approvals` gate **failed** | **25** |\n| CLEAN (approvals already in) | **2** — #321, #329 |\n\n`Approvals` is the only blocking gate anywhere in the project. Five PRs merged since Oct 1.\n\n**#410 caveat:** its `checks` gate reads *\"Gate has not been evaluated yet\"* — I created trail #324 after CI had already finished, so there was no event to evaluate. All 29 checks are green. I'm not pushing the re-trigger because a new head SHA resets its `findings` gate, which currently reads passed.\n\n---\n\n## Linear ↔ trail mapping\n\n`✓` = the PR body cites the issue. `~` = matched on title, not cited.\n\n### In review (25)\n\n| Linear | Trail | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| COR-2007 ✓, COR-2146 ✓ | [308](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/308) | Semantic provider schema 1.3 ingested in full |\n| COR-2153 ~ | [242](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/242) | Retrieval returns output an agent can accept |\n| COR-2158 ✓, COR-2147 ✓ | [313](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/313) | Six compatibility aliases hidden from the MCP surface |\n| COR-2163 ✓, COR-2157 ✓ | [310](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/310) | `brain_recall` over MCP + guard against losing a tool |\n| COR-2162 ✓ | [312](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/312) | Component failure ages out once it rebuilds |\n| COR-2162 ✓ | [311](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/311) | A writer refusing an unknown field is not corruption |\n| COR-2159 ✓ | [315](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/315) | Doctor warns on an install the OS may delete |\n| COR-2002 ✓ | [309](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/309) | Pre-push gate settled, two env-only failures named |\n| COR-2002 ~ | [267](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/267) | Test suite deadline above its own runtime |\n| COR-2029 ✓, COR-2006 ~ | [287](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/287) | Seven-phase setup UI, capability block, distill consent |\n| COR-2006 ~ | [314](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/314) | Setup output short-form by default |\n| COR-2006 ~ | [241](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/241) | Distill timeout configurable, nested-repo trap named |\n| COR-2148 ~ | [286](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/286) | Repo with no captured sessions no longer reported broken |\n| COR-2148 ~ | [260](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/260) | Setup and status say what is true on a first run |\n| COR-2149 ~ | [257](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/257) | Setup makes the brain discoverable, remembers declines |\n| COR-2150 ~ | [264](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/264) | Three remedies the reader could not follow |\n| COR-2150 ~ | [263](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/263) | Remedies in the reader's own dispatch spelling |\n| COR-2150 ~ | [262](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/262) | Printed advice made runnable |\n| COR-2150 ~ | [256](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/256) | Doctor prints only what a reader can act on |\n| COR-2151 ~ | [261](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/261) | Our own installers stop blocking our own install |\n| COR-2152 ~ | [258](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/258) | Memory prepass says why it failed |\n| COR-2155 ~ | [259](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/259) | Bundle says what sharing a brain costs |\n| COR-2157 ~ | [265](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/265) | Changelog since 0.1.0 + integration branch |\n| COR-2029 ✓ | [255](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/255) | Connect fails loudly when hosted binding can't resolve |\n| — | [266](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/266) | Ollama envelope guard bound by the client |\n| **none yet** | [324](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/324) | **Locus extractor path fragmentation** (ashtom, Slack) |\n| COR-2156 ~ | [246](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/246) | *merged* — concurrent-git collision, dirty-tree stall |\n\n**Two gaps worth closing:** trail 324 (the locus fix) and trail 266 (the ollama flake) have no Linear issue. I can file both.\n\n---\n\n## Linear issues left to tackle in brain\n\n### Blocked only on you merging the 25 — no code left\n**COR-2157** Cut a stable release + re-run the outsider install. Milestone M5 says it plainly: an outsider installing today gets a binary **356 commits / 46 merged PRs behind main**. The install path works; the content is stale. *This is the actual P0 exit criterion.*\n\n⚠️ Hazard carried in M5: `v0.2.0`, `v0.3.0`, `v0.3.1` exist as **local-only tags that were never pushed**, and `release.yml` fires on `push: tags: v*`. A stray `git push --tags` publishes from whatever those point at.\n\n### New this morning — watch daemon, 3 of 4 High, nobody on them\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **COR-2174** 🔴 | Upgrading entire-brain silently wedges the watch daemon: every tick fails, distill never runs, status still says ✓ running |\n| **COR-2175** 🔴 | Watch daemon blocks itself — the memory worker it launches holds `write.lock`, so that tick's refresh fails `brain_locked` and skips distill |\n| **COR-2177** 🔴 | Distill re-spends on every branch copy of a session; merged sessions are distilled again from scratch on main |\n| **COR-2176** 🟡 | `watch.log` has no timestamps, and most lines don't say which repo or tick they belong to |\n\nThese four are a coherent cluster and the only High-priority unowned work in the project. **2174 + 2175 together mean the daemon can be silently dead while reporting healthy** — that's the one I'd take first.\n\n### The memory-architecture epic — 11 issues, all Backlog, none started\nCOR-2052 remove Graph from the memory workflow · COR-2053 nonblocking lifecycle notifications · COR-2054 event-driven worker (replaces polling) · COR-2055 incremental, cost-bounded extraction · COR-2056 simplified memory + revision contract · COR-2057 SQLite per repo · COR-2058 preserve history, tighten supersession · COR-2060 revision-aware hosted publication · COR-2061 unify local + hosted retrieval · COR-2062 retire unused subsystems · COR-2154 replace semantic retrieval with BM25 + taxonomy filters\n\nCOR-2059 (remove duplicate transcript storage) is the only one Done. **COR-2056 is the contract the other ten depend on** — it's the right entry point, and COR-2054 is where the new daemon bugs above would be fixed properly rather than patched.\n\n### Quality / bench\n- **COR-2160** CI has two required \"benchmark\" jobs and neither is a regression floor\n- **COR-2161** Land the BrainMark harness fixes before anything is gated on its scores — matches my note that the 2026-08-29 audit found 9 defects, 3 disqualifying\n- **COR-2144** Diagnostic context for intermittent Git fixture HEAD parse failures\n\n### Security\n- **COR-2145** ✅ Done\n- **COR-2164** still Backlog, High, assigned to Alex Ong — I posted the assessment (criticals reach only `scripts/bench` via `node-llama-cpp`, never in CI, never shipped; COR-2154 deletes the tree). **It needs closing, not working.**\n\n### Docs / open\nCOR-2005 docs refresh · COR-2006 simplify setup (partly covered by trails 287/314/241) · COR-2147 agent guides must use commands the released Graph has (partly by trail 313)\n\n---\n\n## Milestones\n\n| | progress |\n|---|---|\n| M1 Harden and GA entire-sem | 8% |\n| M2 Close the brain blockers | 0% ← the 25 PRs land here |\n| M3 GA the MCP surface for both plugins | 25% |\n| M4 brain-bench as the automated eval gate | 0% |\n| M5 Release + distribution | 50% |\n\nM2 reads 0% because nothing has merged. Approving the 25 moves M2 and unblocks M5/COR-2157 in one step.\n\n**If you want me moving while you review:** COR-2174/2175 (the silently-dead daemon) is the highest-value unowned work, and I can file the two missing Linear issues for trails 324 and 266 first."}]}}
