{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"8fe1fe99e31c238cf1c6687f61eac1558ca7c7d5b3741a7128e19965728b2a10","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Today is Monday, so this is **Sun Oct 11 → Mon Oct 19**. 85 PRs across 3 repos: 41 merged, 15 closed as superseded, 29 in review.\n\n```\nOct 11 – Oct 19\n\nlanded the entire-graph launch stack on main — 40 trails merged, 15 superseded\nfinished the P0 brain fix loop: 26 trails in review, all CI green, zero open findings,\nApprovals the only gate left\nfixed ashtom's locus bug — hyphenated and dot paths were cut into fragments\ntwo security assessments closed (setup-go XML parser, argv-parser in bench tooling)\n\nentire-brain  (P0 · GA the Local Brain)\n• :merged: COR-2156 · Brain's git reads stop locking the user's shared index — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/246\n• :review: no issue · Locus extractor cut hyphenated and dot paths into fragments (ashtom) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/324\n• :review: COR-2159 · Doctor warns when the install sits in a directory the OS may delete — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/315\n• :review: COR-2006 · Setup output short-form by default, phases behind --verbose — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/314\n• :review: COR-2158 · Six compatibility aliases hidden from the advertised MCP surface — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/313\n• :review: COR-2162 · A recorded component failure ages out once it rebuilds — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/312\n• :review: COR-2162 · A writer refusing an unknown field is not corruption — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/311\n• :review: COR-2163 · brain_recall over MCP, plus a guard against losing a tool again — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/310\n• :review: COR-2002 · Pre-push gate settled, two env-only failures named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/309\n• :review: COR-2007 · Semantic provider schema 1.3 ingested in full — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/308\n• :review: COR-2006 · Seven-phase setup UI, capability block, distill consent — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/287\n• :review: COR-2148 · A repo with no captured sessions is no longer reported broken — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/286\n• :review: COR-2146 · Provider failure summarised instead of dumping the host CLI's help — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/285\n• :review: COR-2002 · Test suite gets a deadline above its own runtime — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/267\n• :review: no issue · Ollama envelope guard bound by the client, not the writer — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/266\n• :review: COR-2157 · Changelog since 0.1.0 and the integration branch for the fix stack — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/265\n• :review: COR-2150 · Three remedies the reader could not follow — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/264\n• :review: COR-2150 · Remedies rendered in the reader's own dispatch spelling — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/263\n• :review: COR-2150 · Printed advice made runnable, escape hatch named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/262\n• :review: COR-2151 · Our own installers stop blocking our own install — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/261\n• :review: COR-2148 · Setup and status say what is true on a first run — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/260\n• :review: COR-2155 · Bundle says what sharing a brain costs, at the moment it costs it — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/259\n• :review: COR-2152 · Memory prepass says why it failed, stops retrying what can't change — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/258\n• :review: COR-2149 · Setup makes the brain discoverable and remembers a decline — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/257\n• :review: COR-2150 · Doctor prints only what a reader can act on — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/256\n• :review: COR-2029 · Connect fails loudly when the hosted binding can't resolve — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/255\n• :review: COR-2153 · Retrieval returns output an agent can accept, and discloses what was dropped — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/242\n• :review: COR-2006 · Distill timeout configurable, nested-repo trap named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/241\n\nentire-graph  (outside Linear)\n• :merged: Graph launch stack landed on current main — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/262\n• :merged: Agent output diagnostics: subdir VERIFY, warm coverage, edges --cache-dir — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/247\n• :merged: Committed-tree caches reused across queries, worktrees and clones — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/243\n• :merged: Go router group prefix fixed point bounded (hang on labstack/echo) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/226\n• :merged: Declaration-aware output and Go route analysis — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/236\n• :merged: Declarations preserved when trimming tail results — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/238\n• :merged: Related locators point at declaration names — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/237\n• :merged: Exact definitions and indexed route lines preserved — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/244\n• :merged: Exact corpus-wide IDF statistics — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/214\n• :merged: Agent output no longer depends on measured latency — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/222\n• :merged: Multi-pattern git grep hang fixed, git children killed on signal — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/220\n• :merged: Normal result caps preserved across callee and card composition — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/219\n• :merged: Implicit auxiliary results capped at top-k — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/218\n• :merged: Source and primary identity preserved under tight budgets — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/217\n• :merged: Replay bound to its producing revision, heredoc data preserved — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/216\n• :merged: Verification runners require subject evidence — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/215\n• :merged: Agent byte budgets enforced on session replay — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/204\n• :merged: Graph correctness and accounting repairs integrated — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/212\n• :merged: Adaptive agent budget (draft) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/211\n• :merged: A mentioned runner is not an invoked runner — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/210\n• :merged: Savings unfloored, only pipeline heads classified, writes detected — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/200\n• :merged: Observed follow-up reported without false credit — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/245\n• :merged: Ambiguous local calls no longer claimed as exact — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/202\n• :merged: Untracked nested worktrees excluded from the corpus — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/203\n• :merged: Nested callables emitted as phantom type members (Swift, Kotlin, Rust, PHP) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/196\n• :merged: Every relation labelled EXTRACTED, INFERRED or AMBIGUOUS — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/195\n• :merged: complete-symbol surfaced to agents, no longer abbreviated — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/198\n• :merged: Guide asks for --format agent, ~2.9x cheaper per query — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/197\n• :merged: Required reads and installer guide parity preserved — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/206\n• :merged: Opt-in prompt-time graph context hook (Claude Code) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/240\n• :merged: Graph guidance extended, Claude subagent hooks registered — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/242\n• :merged: Cache, route-bound and source-read safeguards enforced — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/241\n• :merged: Cache writes streamed, preindex verified by digest not decode — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/234\n• :merged: Annotation windows scanned without splitting the whole file — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/232\n• :merged: Same-name candidates no longer copied on every lookup — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/231\n• :merged: Windows CI prints per-assignment progress and a heartbeat — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/235\n• :merged: Both statusline platforms finish independently — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/208\n• :merged: Locate bench enforces offline measurement and replay guards — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/207\n• :merged: PyJWT bumped in the memory benchmark lockfile — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/250\n• :merged: README puts setup before benchmarks — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/185\n• :review: Opt-in local semantic retrieval channel — draft, needs a product decision — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/221\n• :review: Wall-clock ceiling on indexing — mitigation; the relation phase is still quadratic — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/102\n\ncli\n• :review: investigate/review error hints point at `entire agent add` (no trail) — https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2292\n```\n\nFour things worth saying out loud about that list:\n\n- **15 entire-graph PRs are `closed`, not abandoned** — #277, #279, #283, #291, #302–#304, #306–#309, #312, #328, #330, #331. They were cherry-picked into the launch stack (trail 262) and closed as superseded. I left them out rather than pad the list with `:x:` rows, but they're real work if anyone asks why the numbers don't line up.\n- **Trail 102 is the one ashtom asked about** — it's still open, from August, and the title is honest that it's a mitigation: the relation phase is still quadratic. Unrelated to his locus report.\n- **Three trails have no Linear issue**: 324 (locus fix), 266 (ollama flake), and cli #2292 has no trail at all. I can file all three.\n- **COR-2029** appears twice above but isn't in the P0 project list — it's cited in the bodies of #340 and #374, so it lives in another project."}]}}
