{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"3bde2a6123b675b59f8ca4f396354554ea17900da32c2c5dc31e6f822c7d9ea7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Setup feedback — **already shipped**, in trail [314](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/314) (short-form output) and [287](https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/287) (the seven-phase UI). Here it is rendered live from the integration branch, on a real PTY in an isolated repo — not a mockup:\n\n**Default (what people actually see now):**\n```\nagent: auto-selected claude-code, model: the agent's own default (SPENDS TOKENS)\n       — override with --agent, pin a model with --model\n\n  Brain turns this repo's history and past AI sessions into memories your\n  agents recall while they work.\n\n  ✓ Brain built — queryable now (584ms)\n  − semantic search unavailable — run `entire plugin install graph`\n  − 1 other component did not build — `entire-brain doctor` names them\n  ✓ No past sessions to distill — memories accrue as you work\n  − Watcher not installed (--no-daemon) — the brain updates only when you re-run setup\n\nReady. Try: entire-brain brief \"<your task>\"\nMemories stay on this machine. To share them: entire-brain connect\n```\n\nFive lines and a next step, down from the wall of phase output. During the run it's a single repainting progress line, not scrollback.\n\n**`--verbose` keeps the whole thing for when you need it:**\n```\n✓ Detect    repo repo · 1 commit · clean tree\n            agent    claude-code (effort low)\n            provider none — entire plugin install graph\n            hosted   not bound — local-only (COR-2029); bind: entire-brain connect\n✓ Build     instant core ready in 800ms — 6 of 8 components built, FAILED semantic…\n            semantic index failed (provider_doctor_failed: semantic provider no-egress…\n            entity index failed (read graph identity revision: Invalid usage: unknown…\n✓ Agents    session-end hook already wired (/Users/suhaan/.claude/settings.json)\n            push hook not installed (run `entire-brain connect` to upload memories on…\n            agent instructions already current (.entire/agent-guide.md, AGENTS.md,…\n            pre-edit hook already wired (…)\n− Facts     no sessions to distill; the brain is queryable now\n✓ Workspace workspace \"default\" already has this repo\n− Watcher   background watcher (--no-daemon)\n✓ Ready     the brain is queryable · 810ms\n            next     entire-brain overview  — what this project is\n            next     entire-brain brief \"<task>\"  — task-shaped context\n            next     entire-brain status  — backfill progress and daemon health\n            next     entire-brain connect  — sync memories with your team (off by…\n```\n\nYou also asked about the other states — those are in: a first run with sessions gets the distill consent block (default **no**, and it never blocks without a terminal), a declined hook is remembered and says so, and `connect` only appears in next-steps when there's no hosted binding.\n\nOne honest gap: I couldn't render the **distill consent prompt** here because the demo repo has no captured sessions, and I won't fake sessions to make a screenshot. It's unit-tested, not eyeballed.\n\n---\n\n## Before I merge — verification state\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Trail findings open | **0** across all 27 — `findings` gate passed on every one |\n| CI | green on all 27 (every Actions check) |\n| Conflicts | none, 27/27 mergeable |\n| `up_to_date` | passed 27/27 |\n| Full `internal/cli` suite | green locally on the locus fix (211s) |\n\n**Merge order:** #395 before #329 (they conflict in `semantic.go`; resolution is in both bodies), #340 closed not merged, integration branch #350 last.\n\n**Linear on merge** — I'll move these to Done: COR-2002, 2006, 2007, 2029, 2146, 2148, 2149, 2150, 2151, 2152, 2153, 2155, 2158, 2159, 2162, 2163, and close **COR-2164** on the assessment already posted. **COR-2157** stays open — it needs the actual v0.2.0 tag cut after the merge, not just the PRs landing.\n\nTwo things I need you to know before you say go:\n\n1. **`approvals` needs a human.** The gate config has `allow_self_approval: true`, so I *can* clear it by approving on your behalf — but that's me approving my own 26 PRs. Tell me explicitly if you want that, or approve them yourself and I'll merge straight after.\n2. **I'll file the two missing Linear issues** for trail 324 (locus) and 266 (ollama flake) so nothing lands unmapped.\n\nSay **good** and I'll run the merge in order, then update Linear."}]}}
