{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"d2eab723ab2343ff8980cc8d4769d5421477eb53c49b6175675dae8a24e61709","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Caught something before merging — this changes the order.\n\n**#401 would regress the consent gate.** Compare how each branch decides whether a human can be asked:\n\n```\n#374:  TTY: setupCanAskAHuman(ui.tty, readerIsTerminal(in))   ← both ends\n#401:  TTY: ui.tty                                            ← stdout only\n```\n\n`setupCanAskAHuman` and `readerIsTerminal` exist **only on #374**. Merging #401 first drops them, and setup would then prompt whenever *stdout* is a terminal while reading from a non-terminal stdin — the exact wedged-pipeline case `consent.go`'s own doc warns about. The two branches share 8 commits but neither contains the other, and both merge orders conflict on the second one.\n\nSo: **#374 first**, then reconcile #401 on top."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UTQ7RDDWJXzGSGuv9SvCP9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-locus-anchors && gh pr checks 374 --repo entireio/entire-brain 2>/dev/null | awk -F'\\t' '$2!=\"pass\"{print $1\"=\"$2}'; echo \"--- required checks all green?\"; gh pr view 374 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json statusCheckRollup --jq '[.statusCheckRollup[]|select(.conclusion!=\"SUCCESS\" and .conclusion!=\"SKIPPED\")|{name:(.name//.context),c:.conclusion}]'","description":"Confirm 374 required checks green"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
