{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"1efc428b7ab1ca76e24da93633498ee9080335b401b105cd2191af009608624d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Full suite green. Committing the resolution and pushing:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U3mqAowsQ33EyB92YHWRef","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-terse-merge && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main (#374) into the terse-output branch\n\nFour conflicts, all of them the same question: which branch already owns this\nbehaviour. Resolved by checking, not by picking a side.\n\n.gitattributes      took main's rules. `*.golden*` is strictly broader than\n                    this branch's `**/testdata/*.golden*`, and no golden\n                    fixture lives outside a testdata directory, so main's\n                    version loses nothing and re-litigates nothing.\n\nsetup.go            kept this branch. Main refreshes the push hook in a flat\n                    block after the watcher; this branch moved it into the\n                    AGENTS phase as refreshSetupPushHook, preserving every\n                    branch of main's logic (sharedDir, absent, unchanged,\n                    chainedIn, refreshed). Taking main's block would refresh\n                    twice and print the hook in two different styles -- which\n                    is what main's own comment there warns against.\n\nsetup_render.go     kept this branch: renderSetupSummary is the long renderer\nsetup_render_test   this PR replaces. Verified no caller, and no reference to\n                    summaryBarWidth or setupSummaryLabelWidth survives.\n\nTwo things the merge did not resolve by itself:\n\n  - setup_render.go's fmt/io/strings imports were used only by the renderer\n    that went away.\n  - setup_consent_stdin_test.go came from #374 calling newSetupSink(progress);\n    this branch's signature takes (progress, quiet). Passed quiet=false so the\n    gate still runs the full prompt path -- a quiet sink could suppress the\n    prompt and quietly stop exercising the read the test exists for.\n\nThe fix that made the order matter is intact: the consent gate still reads\nTTY: setupCanAskAHuman(ui.tty, readerIsTerminal(in)), both ends, not ui.tty.\nVerified by weakening -- reverting it to ui.tty makes\nTestTheBackfillGateDoesNotBlockOnAPipeWithATerminalStdout fail on the 20s\nclock with \"the consent gate read from a pipe that never EOFs\"; restored,\ngreen.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green (359s), setupui and tui green, build and vet clean.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1 && git push -q origin HEAD:feat/setup-output-terse 2>&1 | tail -3 && echo PUSHED","description":"Commit and push the resolved merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
