{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"505472d14c1f6a2e6c3aa3cabdc0a61e37d943856b04a2c43dd6f42a5ca0a395","message":{"role":"system","content":"<total_tokens>14968951 tokens left</total_tokens>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"1fe770564c4e3167ff0d04bec46fcd10b3dd44593a6471b00ced8cad8ae6dca9","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0128rZPF8oL9Qv9GuU7Kocze","name":"mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_issue","input":{"team":"Core","project":"P-COR-39","title":"Fact locus extraction cuts file paths at hyphens and drops leading dots","priority":2,"state":"In Progress","description":"Reported by @ashtom in Slack.\n\nA fact about `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` was anchored to `website/scripts/pre` and `build.ts` — two tokens that name nothing in the repo — while the real path never appeared. Re-recording the fact with the path in backticks did not help: the backtick span added the correct token, but the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it.\n\n## Root cause\n\nOne regex, `locusIdentifierPattern` in `internal/cli/facts_locus.go`. Two cuts of the same class:\n\n1. **No `-` in any segment character class.** A segment ended at the first hyphen and the remainder restarted as a fresh token.\n2. **No leading `.`**, and `factLocus`'s `add()` trimmed its punctuation cutset from *both* ends, so `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was stored as `github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n\n## Why a fragment is worse than a missing anchor\n\nA fragment looks like a path, so it binds the fact to a file that does not exist — and `factLocusDrift` cannot flag it. `locusTokenIsFilePath` requires a slash **and** an extension: `website/scripts/pre` has no extension, `build.ts` has no slash, so neither reaches the `os.Stat`. A hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it would ever be reported as drifted.\n\nThe leading-dot case fails the opposite way: `github/workflows/ci.yml` *does* pass the file-path test and resolves nowhere, so it reads as drifted on every recall, forever.\n\n## Fix\n\nSegments become `[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*` with an optional leading dot. The hyphen must be interior, so a trailing dash stays out of the token, and the first alternative still requires a `.` or `/`, which keeps ordinary hyphenated English (\"state-of-the-art\") out of the locus. `add()` trims leading and trailing punctuation with separate cutsets.\n\nNo migration needed: `reclassify` already rewrites `Locus` when it differs from what the text derives, so stored facts shed their fragments on the next pass.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Tests fail on main with exactly the reported symptom, backticked case included.\n- Verified by weakening: dropping the interior-hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the asymmetric trim each turns them red; all three restored, green.\n- Full `internal/cli` suite green; build and vet clean; 29 CI checks pass.","links":[{"url":"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/324","title":"Trail 324 — locus extractor fix"},{"url":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/410","title":"PR #410"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"87361ab9d06e439d38f09799af378c5c3b684ee3e0b36512d857ab2df6008504","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0128rZPF8oL9Qv9GuU7Kocze","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2180\",\"uuid\":\"210a45e4-74f4-451b-bcdb-9c7a2ac67e3a\",\"title\":\"Fact locus extraction cuts file paths at hyphens and drops leading dots\",\"description\":\"Reported by @ashtom in Slack.\\n\\nA fact about `website/scripts/pre-build.ts` was anchored to `website/scripts/pre` and `build.ts` — two tokens that name nothing in the repo — while the real path never appeared. Re-recording the fact with the path in backticks did not help: the backtick span added the correct token, but the regex sweep still produced the fragments beside it.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nOne regex, `locusIdentifierPattern` in `internal/cli/facts_locus.go`. Two cuts of the same class:\\n\\n1. **No** `-` **in any segment character class.** A segment ended at the first hyphen and the remainder restarted as a fresh token.\\n2. **No leading** `.`, and `factLocus`'s `add()` trimmed its punctuation cutset from *both* ends, so `.github/workflows/ci.yml` was stored as `github/workflows/ci.yml`.\\n\\n## Why a fragment is worse than a missing anchor\\n\\nA fragment looks like a path, so it binds the fact to a file that does not exist — and `factLocusDrift` cannot flag it. `locusTokenIsFilePath` requires a slash **and** an extension: `website/scripts/pre` has no extension, `build.ts` has no slash, so neither reaches the `os.Stat`. A hyphenated file could be deleted and no fact about it would ever be reported as drifted.\\n\\nThe leading-dot case fails the opposite way: `github/workflows/ci.yml` *does* pass the file-path test and resolves nowhere, so it reads as drifted on every recall, forever.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nSegments become `[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:-[A-Za-z0-9_]+)*` with an optional leading dot. The hyphen must be interior, so a trailing dash stays out of the token, and the first alternative still requires a `.` or `/`, which keeps ordinary hyphenated English (\\\"state-of-the-art\\\") out of the locus. `add()` trims leading and trailing punctuation with separate cutsets.\\n\\nNo migration needed: `reclassify` already rewrites `Locus` when it differs from what the text derives, so stored facts shed their fragments on the next pass.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n* Tests fail on main with exactly the reported symptom, backticked case included.\\n* Verified by weakening: dropping the interior-hyphen groups, the leading dot, or the asymmetric trim each turns them red; all three restored, green.\\n* Full `internal/cli` suite green; build and vet clean; 29 CI checks pass.\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2180/fact-locus-extraction-cuts-file-paths-at-hyphens-and-drops-leading\",\"gitBranchName\":\"suhaan/cor-2180-fact-locus-extraction-cuts-file-paths-at-hyphens-and-drops\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T14:44:18.934Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T14:44:18.934Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-19T14:44:19.054Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[{\"id\":\"61b3c9b1-7ada-405f-83e6-6afcb189d31a\",\"title\":\"Trail 324 — locus extractor fix\",\"subtitle\":\"Host code and agent sessions together on a fast, distributed Git network. Give your agents the context to understand, collaborate, and ship.\",\"url\":\"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/324\"},{\"id\":\"6574afe4-4035-4f72-ac7f-efd94e3b8358\",\"title\":\"PR #410\",\"subtitle\":null,\"url\":\"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/410\"}],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\",\"createdById\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}]}]}}
