{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"1cc7f78ef25a83df2329704a8e1c24847c4c532ac59e4d598ee69cf8e88f1102","message":{"role":"system","content":"<total_tokens>14957427 tokens left</total_tokens>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"e8740ffc812d9ecf68a2073c4a6e5fdbade3c9ba5dc4a55c72bbc8d6f26e7e29","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#374 is merged.** #401's conflicts are resolved, pushed, and CI is on the last three macOS jobs. Summary while that finishes:\n\n## What happened\n\nYou asked me to merge \"the setup PRs\" — that's **#374** (seven-phase UI, consent gate) and **#401** (short-form output). They couldn't just be merged in sequence.\n\n**The catch I found first:** #401 sets the consent gate's TTY check to `ui.tty` — *stdout only*. #374 sets it to `setupCanAskAHuman(ui.tty, readerIsTerminal(in))` — **both ends**. Those helpers exist only on #374. Merging #401 first would have silently shipped a setup that prompts whenever stdout looks like a terminal while reading from a pipe that never EOFs. That's the wedged-CI case `consent.go`'s own doc warns about in capitals.\n\nSo: #374 first (clean), then reconcile #401.\n\n## The four conflicts, and how each was decided\n\n| file | kept | why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.gitattributes` | **main's** | `*.golden*` is strictly broader than `**/testdata/*.golden*`, and I checked — no golden fixture lives outside a `testdata/` dir. Main's loses nothing. |\n| `setup.go` | **#401's** | Main refreshes the push hook in a flat block after the watcher; #401 moved it into the AGENTS phase as `refreshSetupPushHook`, preserving all five branches. Taking main's would refresh twice — which main's *own comment* warns against. |\n| `setup_render.go` | **#401's** | `renderSetupSummary` is the long renderer this PR replaces. Verified zero callers and no surviving reference to `summaryBarWidth` / `setupSummaryLabelWidth`. |\n| `setup_render_test.go` | **#401's** | Same block's tests. |\n\nTwo things the merge couldn't resolve itself: `setup_render.go`'s `fmt`/`io`/`strings` imports were used only by the deleted renderer, and #374's `setup_consent_stdin_test.go` calls `newSetupSink(progress)` against #401's `(progress, quiet)` signature. I passed `quiet=false` so the gate still runs the full prompt path — a quiet sink could suppress the prompt and quietly stop exercising the read the test exists for.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **The fix survived**: `TTY: setupCanAskAHuman(ui.tty, readerIsTerminal(in))` is intact post-merge\n- **Verified by weakening**: reverted it to `ui.tty` → `TestTheBackfillGateDoesNotBlockOnAPipeWithATerminalStdout` failed on the 20s clock with *\"the consent gate read from a pipe that never EOFs\"*. Restored → green.\n- Full `internal/cli` **359s green**, `setupui` + `tui` green, build and vet clean\n- Windows shards 0–7 all green on CI; macOS is the long pole (it runs ~17–20min against a 20min cap)\n\n## Linear\n\nFiled the two trails that had no issue, both in P0:\n- **[COR-2180](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2180/fact-locus-extraction-cuts-file-paths-at-hyphens-and-drops-leading)** — ashtom's locus bug (High), linked to trail 324 + PR #410\n- **[COR-2181](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2181/ollama-envelope-test-measured-the-fake-servers-own-cap-not-the-client)** — ollama envelope flake (Medium), linked to trail 266\n\nOne correction to what I told you earlier: **COR-2029 is already Done and lives in P1**, not P0 — it's the CLI `repo view --json` work. The brain PRs only cite it as context, so there's nothing to move there. I'll hold COR-2006 open until #321 lands too, since it's tagged on that as well.\n\nI'll merge #401 and update Linear as soon as macOS finishes."}]}}
