{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"2519991bb56b5b49b83ff0b77a42f4f9fa07786ecf51a407654de8e13677e855","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Five merged today: #374, #401, #410, #398, #352.** Then the permission classifier started refusing again — it allowed four merges in a row and blocked #396. It's gating intermittently, and I'm not going to try to route around it.\n\n## Where it stands\n\n**Merged** — the setup output work (#374 + #401), ashtom's locus fix (#410), manifest refusal wording (#398), CI test deadline (#352).\n\n**Verified ready, blocked on permission** — 11 more from the clean set, in this order:\n\n```\n396  351  343  397  402  321  400  395  344  399  347  346\n```\n\nThese are not guesses. I replayed every one against `main` in a throwaway worktree, built the cumulative tree, and ran it: `go build ./...` clean, `go vet ./...` clean, **`internal/cli` full suite green at 289s**, every other package green. The order already puts **#395 before #329**.\n\n**Needs reconciling after those land** — 8 PRs, and I now know exactly why each conflicts:\n\n| PR | conflicts | cause |\n|---|---|---|\n| #373 | 1 hunk | references the long renderer #401 deleted |\n| #341 | 1 hunk | `distill_cmd.go` only |\n| #372 | 2 hunks | `setup.go` phase wiring |\n| #348 / #349 | 5 / 3 hunks | overlap *each other* in `blind_spot.go` + `publish.go` + `semantic.go` |\n| #342 | 6 hunks | long renderer |\n| #345 | 10 hunks | long renderer |\n| #329 | 15 hunks, 8 files | the big one; needs #395 in first |\n\nSix of the eight are the same mechanical cause. They have to be resolved against the real post-merge `main`, not my simulation — otherwise I'd be merging unlanded commits into branches.\n\n**#340** is confirmed **+0/-0 across 0 files** and just needs closing. `gh pr close` was separately refused as *External System Writes*.\n\n## What unblocks this\n\nAdd permission rules for `Bash(gh pr merge:*)` and `Bash(gh pr close:*)` — via `/permissions`, or `! claude config` if you prefer. Then I'll land the 11, reconcile the 8 the same way I did #401 (resolve, verify by weakening, full suite, push), close #340, and move Linear.\n\nLinear is untouched so far — deliberately. I'll move COR-2002, 2006, 2007, 2146, 2148, 2149, 2150, 2151, 2152, 2153, 2155, 2158, 2159, 2162, 2163, 2180, 2181 to Done and close COR-2164 **once their PRs are actually in**, not before. **COR-2157 stays open** either way: it needs the v0.2.0 tag cut, and the unpushed local `v0.2.0`/`v0.3.0`/`v0.3.1` tags are still a live hazard for anyone who runs `git push --tags`."}]}}
