{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"49e628b5969a286b001cd3623e65c8b28f07afe3c14930904f91b93ae0caf3b7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ffy6FZZZwLHAzPPTJtbYC6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-followable && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q --amend -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main, then #348, into the followable-remedies branch\n\nmain brought four conflicts.\n\npublish.go   -> main. This branch still carried the ENTIRE_BRAIN_ALLOW_HOSTED\n             gate; main retired it in c6c3eed3 (COR-2111/COR-2116). Checked the\n             history, not the diff, before dropping this side.\n\nsemantic.go  -> main's STRUCTURE with this branch's TEXT, in all three hunks.\n             Main had restructured the doctor-failure switch from `return` to\n             `err = ...` so semanticProviderAbsentError can wrap it; returning\n             early, as this branch did, would have skipped that wrapping. Main\n             also gates the live provider probe behind `audit`. Both kept.\n             What this branch contributes is the remedy wording, and that is\n             what went in on top.\n\n             Hunk 2 is the subtle one: main already appends a \"provider is not\n             installed\" clause, with `scripts/install.sh` from a checkout as\n             the remedy, and it already guards against stacking a second one.\n             This branch's extra append would have duplicated it, sat after a\n             return, and referenced an out-of-scope variable. So the block\n             stays and its remedy becomes `entire plugin install graph`.\n\nollama test  -> this branch, which carries #351's named constants\n             (ollamaEnvelopeStreamHeadroom/StopTolerance) and the comment\n             naming the root cause: the old bound sat INSIDE the fake server's\n             own cap, so it measured goroutine scheduling. Same 64MiB headroom\n             as main, tighter 16MiB tolerance.\n\nThen this PR's own test caught my resolution: TestProviderRemediesNameAnInstallThatExists\nrejected \"point --graph-binary at the entire-graph binary to use\", because no\ncommand the reader is running accepts that flag. That is precisely the class of\nunfollowable remedy this PR removes, and I had kept it from main's side by\nmistake. Dropped.\n\n#348 is merged in on top for the same reason this branch already carries #351:\nits guard, TestNoHardcodedBrainSpellingInPrintedRemedies, fails here on the\neight sites main added after both branches were cut, and #348 is where those\nfixes live. #348 merges first.\n\nVerified by weakening: restoring the --graph-binary remedy makes\nTestProviderRemediesNameAnInstallThatExists fail; restored, green. Full\ninternal/cli suite green (0 failing), go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/followable-remedies 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Amend and push 349"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
