{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"b0689f0bea0e9915afa181e467045ff2f549817979c17890ad0eaa8b3f978046","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015PGQVoRHbF8UVD327Ayp9w","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-b-agentwiring && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"internal/cli/setup.go\"); s = p.read_text()\n# Hunks 1 and 2: both sides add different fields / flags. Union.\nfor _ in range(2):\n    a = s.index(\"<<<<<<< HEAD\\n\"); b = s.index(\"=======\\n\", a); c = s.index(\">>>>>>> origin/main\\n\", b)\n    head = s[a+len(\"<<<<<<< HEAD\\n\"):b]; main = s[b+len(\"=======\\n\"):c]\n    s = s[:a] + head + main + s[c+len(\">>>>>>> origin/main\\n\"):]\np.write_text(s); print(\"struct fields and flags: union of both sides\")\nPY\ngofmt -w internal/cli/setup.go && echo \"=== now wire the details into main's agents phase:\"; sed -n '880,900p' internal/cli/setup.go","description":"Union the fields and flags, inspect the call site"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"dd2a2d928c3894c8c14d0873b9ec3be73e77491b36a352b3e920eb1fafe9e1b4","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015PGQVoRHbF8UVD327Ayp9w","type":"tool_result","content":"struct fields and flags: union of both sides\n=== now wire the details into main's agents phase:\n\treportSetupAgents(progress, report.Agents, &report, setupOpts.noAgentHooks, brainCmd)\n\n\treport.Facts = factsBackfillStatusForBrain(storage.BrainDir)\n\n\t// Phase 3 — AGENTS. The hooks that make every later session feed the brain\n\t// without anyone remembering to run anything.\n\tagentsPhase := run.Begin(setupui.PhaseAgents)\n\tagentsPhase.Step(\"session-end hook\")\n\treport.Hook = inspectSessionEndHook(repoDir)\n\thookLine, hookWired := setupHookSummary(report.Hook, rend.Dash())\n\n\t// The push hook rides this phase for the reason the phase exists: both\n\t// hooks are wiring that makes later work reach the brain without anyone\n\t// remembering to run anything. It arrived on main as a flat block after\n\t// the watcher; it depends on nothing the watcher does, so it belongs\n\t// beside the hook it is a sibling of rather than in a row of its own.\n\tagentsPhase.Step(\"push hook\")\n\tpushDetails := refreshSetupPushHook(ctx, opts, repoDir, brainCmd)\n\n\tif hookWired {\n\t\tagentsPhase.OK(hookLine, pushDetails...)","is_error":false}]}}
