{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"c6de75b4d1bbb94229a9065bd9214b47add049af8b032e2bf1616236c9d175d6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"**Fix 1** — the phase keys its marker only on the session-end hook, so wiring the pre-edit hook lands under a \"skipped\" phase. Making the phase report done when any of its wiring did work:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RdnFakMgJUye7EjMKhNWDZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-b-agentwiring && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"internal/cli/setup.go\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"\tphaseDetails := append(append([]string{}, pushDetails...), agentDetails...)\n\tif hookWired {\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"\tphaseDetails := append(append([]string{}, pushDetails...), agentDetails...)\n\t// Wiring is WORK, and a phase that did work must not report \"skipped\".\n\t// The session-end hook is not the only wiring here: writing the agent\n\t// instructions or merging the pre-edit hook is the step that makes the\n\t// brain discoverable at all, so a run that did either reports done.\n\tagentWiringDidWork := report.Agents.Installed && (report.Agents.HookChanged || len(report.Agents.Changed) > 0)\n\tif hookWired || agentWiringDidWork {\"\"\"\nassert old in s\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1)); print(\"phase reports done when any wiring did work\")\nPY\nenv -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go build ./... 2>&1|head -3; env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestWiringTheHookIsReportedAsDoneNotSkipped' -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 2>&1 | grep -E \"_test.go:|FAIL|ok \" | head -4","description":"Make the phase report done for wiring work","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
