{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"0826f1c23c9ec09ee43a4eca58ef1960fe420c1c06b1d7404df92ac16ba7c32e","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Hard weakening didn't compile, so it proved nothing. Let me extract the condition so it's directly testable rather than claiming unverified coverage:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0132P3YLXg4XKjVFf6HuyDRT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-b-agentwiring && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"internal/cli/setup.go\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"\t// Wiring is WORK, and a phase that did work must not report \"skipped\".\n\t// The session-end hook is not the only wiring here: writing the agent\n\t// instructions or merging the pre-edit hook is the step that makes the\n\t// brain discoverable at all, so a run that did either reports done.\n\tagentWiringDidWork := report.Agents.Installed && (report.Agents.HookChanged || len(report.Agents.Changed) > 0)\n\tif hookWired || agentWiringDidWork {\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"\tif setupAgentsPhaseDidWork(hookWired, report.Agents) {\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\n\nanchor = \"func setupAgentsPhaseDetails(\"\nassert anchor in s\nhelper = '''// setupAgentsPhaseDidWork reports whether the AGENTS phase actually did\n// something, which decides its mark.\n//\n// Wiring is WORK, and a phase that did work must not report \"skipped\" -- that\n// is the contradiction this PR exists to remove. The session-end hook is not\n// the only wiring in the phase: writing the agent instructions, or merging the\n// pre-edit hook, is the step that makes the brain discoverable at all. A run\n// that did either on a repo whose session-end hook was already absent still\n// did work, and saying \"skipped\" there denies it.\nfunc setupAgentsPhaseDidWork(hookWired bool, agents setupAgentsState) bool {\n\tif hookWired {\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\treturn agents.Installed && (agents.HookChanged || len(agents.Changed) > 0)\n}\n\n'''\ns = s.replace(anchor, helper + anchor, 1)\np.write_text(s); print(\"condition extracted to setupAgentsPhaseDidWork\")\nPY\ngofmt -w internal/cli/setup.go; env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go build ./... 2>&1|head -3; echo \"build=$?\"","description":"Extract the phase-work condition","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
