{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"c0716a6dc518e1e1b9a19cf30e4908136148f91ebed24be9f5683c27ef87b7e6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0171Lwvi48rdQzEwRaeDTeFM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-b-agentwiring && env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test $(go list ./... | grep -v '/internal/cli$') -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 2>&1 | grep -vE \"^ok|no test files\" | head -5; echo \"others-ok\"; git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into the setup-wires-agents branch\n\nThis is a re-landing, not a conflict resolution. Main's AGENTS phase inspects\nthe session-end hook and refreshes the push hook; it does NOT write agent\ninstructions at all, and has no report.Agents, no agentsWired and no\ninit-agents next step. Checked main for each before touching anything -- this\nPR's feature is genuinely absent upstream, not superseded.\n\nWhat moved, and why:\n\n  reportSetupAgents -> setupAgentsPhaseDetails. It returns rows plus the\n  warning instead of printing, so the rows hang off the AGENTS phase the way\n  main hangs the push hook, and the warning still reaches report.Warnings,\n  which is what --json and the closing summary read. All three pre-edit hook\n  states stay distinct: wired, already wired, and a remembered decline.\n\n  setupNextSteps gained agentsWired and leads with init-agents when the wiring\n  did not land. Every other step assumes an agent can find this brain; until\n  init-agents runs, none can, so naming it third would bury the only step that\n  matters.\n\n  setup_render.go / setup_render_test.go -> main. The long renderer this\n  branch extended is the one #401 deleted; verified no reference to\n  renderSetupSummary, summaryBarWidth or setupAgentsValue survives.\n\n  Struct fields and flags -> union, then deduped: both sides registered\n  no-daemon, uninstall-daemon and no-backfill, which panics pflag at init\n  (\"setup flag redefined\"). Kept this branch's wording, which names the\n  remembered decline.\n\nTwo defects the merge exposed, both real:\n\n  --backfill was read nowhere. Main replaced the remembered-decline path with\n  the consent gate, and setupConsentOverride only knew --no-backfill and --yes.\n  A user who declined once and then typed the documented way back in got\n  silence. --backfill now answers the gate yes.\n\n  The agents phase took its mark from the session-end hook alone, so a run that\n  wrote the agent instructions on a repo with no session-end hook reported\n  \"skipped\" for work it had just done -- the exact contradiction this PR\n  removes, reintroduced through the back door. Extracted as\n  setupAgentsPhaseDidWork and covered directly.\n\nTestWiringTheHookIsReportedAsDoneNotSkipped asserted the word \"skipped\" on the\nhook's own line. The phase renderer marks with a GLYPH on the phase line, so\nthat assertion passed on every run and tested nothing. Moved onto the mark\ncolumn via setupRenderedPhaseMark; the invariant is unchanged.\n\nVerified by weakening: stubbing setupAgentsPhaseDidWork's agent branch to false\nturns two subtests red; dropping init-agents from setupNextSteps turns the\nordering test red. Both restored, green. Full internal/cli suite green (0\nfailing), every other package green, go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/setup-wires-agents 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Verify other packages and push 342","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
