{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"d9dfa2e6727619a9d8facf54204a9fa72afce414fbba9a4027aa470dd9583b35","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"These test hint dedup, which lives in `setupComponentFailureDetails` (phase details), not the terse block. Pointing them at the function that owns the claim:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XMqqpy2YXCEsD15ZFA8zj6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-a-output && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"internal/cli/setup_status_output_truth_test.go\"); s = p.read_text()\n\nold1 = '''\tout := renderSetupSummaryPlain(t, report, &setupTimings{})\n\n\tif !strings.Contains(out, \"refusing to seed\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"refusing to index\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"both failures must still be named, so this guard is not vacuous:\\\\n%s\", out)\n\t}\n\tif n := strings.Count(out, \"hint: \"); n != 1 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"one remedy, one appearance; printed %d times:\\\\n%s\", n, out)\n\t}'''\nnew1 = '''\t// Hints are PHASE DETAILS, not terse-block rows: the terse block counts\n\t// failures and sends the reader to doctor. setupComponentFailureDetails is\n\t// where the dedup lives, so it is asserted there rather than through a\n\t// renderer that never prints a hint at all.\n\t_, failed := partitionSetupComponents(report.Instant.Components)\n\tout := strings.Join(setupComponentFailureDetails(failed, \"--\", setupBrainBinaryName), \"\\\\n\")\n\n\tif !strings.Contains(out, \"refusing to seed\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"refusing to index\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"both failures must still be named, so this guard is not vacuous:\\\\n%s\", out)\n\t}\n\tif n := strings.Count(out, \"hint: \"); n != 1 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"one remedy, one appearance; printed %d times:\\\\n%s\", n, out)\n\t}'''\nassert old1 in s\ns = s.replace(old1, new1, 1)\n\nold2 = '''\tout := renderSetupSummaryPlain(t, report, &setupTimings{})\n\tif n := strings.Count(out, \"hint: \"); n != 2 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"distinct remedies must both appear, got %d:\\\\n%s\", n, out)\n\t}'''\nnew2 = '''\t_, failed := partitionSetupComponents(report.Instant.Components)\n\tout := strings.Join(setupComponentFailureDetails(failed, \"--\", setupBrainBinaryName), \"\\\\n\")\n\tif n := strings.Count(out, \"hint: \"); n != 2 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"distinct remedies must both appear, got %d:\\\\n%s\", n, out)\n\t}'''\nassert old2 in s\ns = s.replace(old2, new2, 1)\np.write_text(s); print(\"both remedy tests retargeted at setupComponentFailureDetails\")\nPY\nenv -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestTheSetupSummaryStatesOneRemedyOnce|TestTwoDifferentRemediesAreBothShown' -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAIL:|ok \" | head -3","description":"Retarget the two remedy tests","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
