{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"ee6411bc3c3285a42f4c4449508fcb17610720b228ffb6f81b1849fa9c590f42","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RN8ZMXmBo1SK9vJgZ45Rnv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-a-output && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into the setup-status-output-truth branch\n\nAnother re-landing. Four files conflicted; the renderer this PR extended is\nthe one #401 deleted, so most of the work was moving each claim onto the\nsurface that now carries it.\n\nsetup.go, 5 hunks:\n\n  Build line   -> main's phase call, with THIS branch's queryability guard.\n                Main asserted \"the brain is queryable now\" unconditionally.\n                Extracted as setupQueryabilityClause so it can be tested.\n  Daemon, x3   -> main's setupDaemonOutcome. Main's side also carries the\n                persistent-service/unit-path detail this branch lacks, so\n                taking main loses nothing and gains that.\n  Nested cmd   -> TEED, not chosen between. Main sends the nested refresh's\n                stderr to the phase sink; this branch captured it so genuine\n                warnings (a coordinator that could not launch, a skipped\n                entity index) could be re-emitted. Sending it to one of the\n                two is how either the rendering or the warnings go missing,\n                so newSetupInstantCommand now takes the sink and writes\n                stderr to io.MultiWriter(sink, &captured).\n\nsetup_render.go / _test.go -> main. renderSetupSummary and its feeders\n(phaseTiming, setupComponentRow, setupDaemonValue, setupPhaseValue) are the\ndeleted renderer; verified none survives.\n\nsetup_firstrun_test.go -> this branch, whose exactly-once guard is strictly\nstronger than main's presence check.\n\nThe 568-line test file then had to be retargeted, because its helpers lived in\nthe deleted renderer's test block. Rebuilt rather than dropped -- these tests\nassert substance, not layout, and every claim still applies to what a reader\nsees. Where it moved:\n\n  component naming      -> setupComponentCountSummary. Asserting it through the\n                        rendered block was a substring search over prose:\n                        \"sessions\" appears in the standing intro sentence, so\n                        it passed on output naming nothing.\n  hint dedup, x2        -> setupComponentFailureDetails, where the seenHints\n                        guard actually lives. The terse block prints no hints.\n  unqueryable headline  -> the terse block's own rows. It names the lost\n                        CAPABILITY (\"semantic search unavailable\"), not the\n                        component id; verbose and doctor carry the names.\n  nested-stream test    -> asserts the tee BEHAVIOURALLY. Identity cannot be\n                        checked through a MultiWriter, and a type check would\n                        pass on a tee to the wrong pair of writers.\n\nOne premise of this PR is superseded and was adopted rather than preserved.\nIt asserted exit 0 for an unqueryable brain (\"one component built, so it is\nworth keeping\"). `setup --help` on main now states the opposite contract\noutright: exit 0 whenever the brain is QUERYABLE, meaning the semantic index,\nthe seed baseline or the history index built. Session export is none of them.\nThe test now asserts the half that stands -- whatever the exit code, setup\nmust not claim queryability it lacks, and must name what is missing.\n\nVerified by weakening: removing the queryability guard, and un-teeing the\nnested stderr, each turn their tests red; both restored, green. The first\nweakening initially fired nothing, which is why the clause was extracted --\nno test reached the --verbose phase line. Full internal/cli suite green (0\nfailing), every other package green, go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/setup-status-output-truth 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Commit and push 345"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
