{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"979f520b57c1ee046ac5a93cd2d7304fb113f8c36153703e8cbed25aee30fc3d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014pZZSvQm2rro2FFj4rRA3T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into the retrieval-output-correctness branch\n\nTwo conflicts, both the long renderer #401 deleted (renderSetupSummary and its\nfeeders). Checked the branch's side for anything of this PR's first -- nothing\nretrieval-related in it -- then took main. No reference to renderSetupSummary\nsurvives.\n\nRemoving it orphaned setup_names_init_agents_test.go, which renders that\nsummary. That test asserts the init-agents Next-block row, which is #342's\nfeature, not this one: this branch touches no agent wiring. The feature and its\nguard now live on fix/setup-wires-agents as\nTestNextStepsLeadWithInitAgentsWhenWiringDidNotLand, so the duplicate goes\nrather than being retargeted here, where it would assert a behaviour this\nbranch does not provide.\n\nOne cross-PR collision, and it is neither PR's bug.\n#398's TestWriterRefusalExplainsItselfInsteadOfSayingCorrupt writes a manifest\ncarrying an \"unknown\" field to prove the reader drops it and the writer refuses\nit. The name it picked was \"suppressed_warnings\" -- which THIS PR adds as a\nreal manifest field, because disclosing what was dropped is the point of it.\nThe test was asserting \"unknown\" about a name the product was still free to\ntake, so it went red the moment the product took it. Repointed at\n\"zz_field_no_release_will_define\", which no release will claim.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green (0 failing), every other package green, go vet\n./... clean.\n\nNote for the merge order: this branch and #395 both touch semantic.go. They do\nnot conflict against main as it stands, because #395 is not in yet. #395 merges\nFIRST; if that resolution is non-trivial it is written into both PR bodies.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/retrieval-output-correctness 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Commit and push 329"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
