{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"d4f581e3cb7bf82f379310c99681de8aecf7c919a0770b36469372c20a45fbf6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MxQ5u6bff5xZPZas2HSwwA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-b-agentwiring && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(setup): say what init-agents writes, not just that it exists\n\nCarried over from setup_names_init_agents_test.go, which #329 retired when the\nrenderer it tested was deleted. That test made three claims about the Next\nblock: init-agents appears, it comes FIRST, and it says what it writes. The\nfirst two were already held here; the third was not, and the row's wording did\nnot satisfy it.\n\nThe reported case is why the third matters: a user ran setup, saw it succeed,\nfound no AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md and concluded they had run it from the wrong\ndirectory. They had not -- the step simply was not named anywhere they were\nlooking. \"tell agents this brain exists\" does not tell them a file is missing\nor which one.\n\nVerified by weakening: reverting the row to the old wording turns the\nassertion red. Full internal/cli suite green.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/setup-wires-agents 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Push the 342 follow-up"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
