{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"5c641ef35004249079ef0840c59a4ea09e127d5d3a50d1cd75f85c266cf57cef","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LFr88JCPD98LfdVooiLKXD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-fix-373 && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"internal/cli/setup_terse.go\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = '''\tbrainComponentDocs:     \"docs search\",\n}'''\nnew = '''\tbrainComponentDocs:     \"docs search\",\n\t// Session export earns a label for one reason: its commonest failure is\n\t// not a failure. A repository where no agent session has finished yet\n\t// reports an incomplete scope and no readable IDs, which is exactly what\n\t// every repository looks like before its first session. Left unlabelled it\n\t// collapsed into \"1 other component did not build -- doctor names them\",\n\t// so the reader ran doctor to be told nothing was wrong. That round trip\n\t// is the referral loop this PR removes, and it has to be closed in the\n\t// SHORT form, because the short form is what they see.\n\tbrainComponentSessions: \"session history\",\n}'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\n\nold2 = '''\tbrainComponentSemantic: \"run `entire plugin install graph`\",\n}'''\nnew2 = '''\tbrainComponentSemantic: \"run `entire plugin install graph`\",\n\t// Not a command: there is nothing to run. The honest remedy for \"no\n\t// captured sessions yet\" is to work, which is why this one is a sentence.\n\tbrainComponentSessions: \"no captured sessions yet — they accrue as you work in this repo\",\n}'''\nassert old2 in s\np.write_text(s.replace(old2, new2, 1)); print(\"session history labelled, with the expected-state explanation\")\nPY\nenv -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestEgressAllowedNoSessionsIsNotSentBackToRefresh' -p 1 -parallel 1 -count=1 2>&1 | sed -n '/setup must explain/,/^FAIL/p' | head -14","description":"La