{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"a7d5b945fd11594c1bcd94622f7f1a3de85144fd366d1c96c692c005634ef69d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed intermittent (COR-2144), not mine. Pushing #373's fix:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011LjUpeEfgynsqMggWtwoJ2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-fix-373 && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(setup): name the no-sessions state in the SHORT form, not only in doctor\n\nCI caught what my merge of main did not: the explanation this PR adds lives in\nthe phase details, and the short form is now the default. A first run with no\ncaptured sessions collapsed to\n\n    - 1 other component did not build — `entire-brain doctor` names them\n\nso the reader ran doctor to be told that nothing was wrong. That round trip is\nthe referral loop this PR exists to remove, and closing it only in the verbose\npath closes it where nobody was looking.\n\nSession export earns a terse label for one reason: its commonest failure is not\na failure. A repository where no agent session has finished yet reports an\nincomplete scope and no readable IDs, which is exactly what every repository\nlooks like before its first session. Its remedy is a sentence rather than a\ncommand, because there is no command -- the honest answer is to work.\n\nMy own process gap, stated plainly: this is the one branch of the eight where I\nran targeted tests instead of the full package before pushing, and this is the\ntest that would have caught it.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green. TestBrainBriefGitIntentLiveShapedOperationalRecall\nfailed once with \"fatal: could not parse HEAD\" and passed alone, on main, and on\na second full run -- that is the intermittent git-fixture flake tracked as\nCOR-2144, not this change.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/brain-nosessions-loop 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]|cannot lock ref|another git process\" | tail -2","description":"Push 373's fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
