{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"0de12de5e4e62d0de8a7bded10584a8839aff092fa5f9d891c55feb11bbd5ef8","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Pre-existing isolation debt in files I never touched, surfaced only by `-shuffle=on` (CI doesn't shuffle). Filing it rather than silently sitting on it:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L4UCqKD4iij8mXedMxeh8Y","name":"mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_issue","input":{"team":"Core","project":"P-COR-39","title":"internal/cli has order-dependent tests that only fail under -shuffle=on","priority":3,"description":"Found while verifying the October merge stack. The suite is green in declaration order (local and CI), but `go test ./internal/cli/ -shuffle=on` fails reproducibly:\n\n| run | failing |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `TestDefaultEmbedderLoads`, `TestGlobalFactsNeverEnterARepositorysVectorCache`, `TestMCPRetrievalCanExcludeGlobalFactsPerRequest` |\n| 2 | `TestHookSessionEndRecordsRecoveryHintAfterExportFailure` (+2 subtests) |\n| 3 | same as run 2 |\n\nThese live in `embed_test.go`, `facts_global_test.go` and `hook_lifecycle_regression_test.go` — none of which the merge stack touched, so this is pre-existing, not a regression.\n\n**Why it matters:** CI does not shuffle, so this is invisible there. It means some tests pass because an earlier test left process-global state behind (likely an embedder singleton and a vector-cache path). A test that passes for the wrong reason is the same class of problem as a test that asserts nothing — and it will surface as an unexplained CI failure the first time sharding or parallelism changes the order.\n\n**Suggested fix:** run `-shuffle=on` in one CI job so the order dependence is caught where it is introduced, then isolate the offending globals (the embedder loader and the per-repo vector cache are the likely candidates).\n\nRelated: COR-2144 tracks a separate intermittent git-fixture `could not parse HEAD` failure in the same package."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"8553e997e9a82f3468ccd146268f6d7716b45ad1f3a70fc6c36a5340b33ddfa5","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L4UCqKD4iij8mXedMxeh8Y","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2183\",\"uuid\":\"de7ebe77-904c-42f0-8138-2a74232b2048\",\"title\":\"internal/cli has order-dependent tests that only fail under -shuffle=on\",\"description\":\"Found while verifying the October merge stack. The suite is green in declaration order (local and CI), but `go test ./internal/cli/ -shuffle=on` fails reproducibly:\\n\\n| run | failing |\\n| -- | -- |\\n| 1 | `TestDefaultEmbedderLoads`, `TestGlobalFactsNeverEnterARepositorysVectorCache`, `TestMCPRetrievalCanExcludeGlobalFactsPerRequest` |\\n| 2 | `TestHookSessionEndRecordsRecoveryHintAfterExportFailure` (+2 subtests) |\\n| 3 | same as run 2 |\\n\\nThese live in `embed_test.go`, `facts_global_test.go` and `hook_lifecycle_regression_test.go` — none of which the merge stack touched, so this is pre-existing, not a regression.\\n\\n**Why it matters:** CI does not shuffle, so this is invisible there. It means some tests pass because an earlier test left process-global state behind (likely an embedder singleton and a vector-cache path). A test that passes for the wrong reason is the same class of problem as a test that asserts nothing — and it will surface as an unexplained CI failure the first time sharding or parallelism changes the order.\\n\\n**Suggested fix:** run `-shuffle=on` in one CI job so the order dependence is caught where it is introduced, then isolate the offending globals (the embedder loader and the per-repo vector cache are the likely candidates).\\n\\nRelated: <issue id=\\\"ac875fa4-398b-45ad-b9a5-21e70bb42a39\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2144/capture-diagnostic-context-for-intermittent-git-fixture-head-parse\\\">COR-2144</issue> tracks a separate intermittent git-fixture `could not parse HEAD` failure in the same package.\",\"priority\":{\"value\":3,\"name\":\"Medium\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2183/internalcli-has-order-dependent-tests-that-only-fail-under-shuffleon\",\"gitBranchName\":\"suhaan/cor-2183-internalcli-has-order-dependent-tests-that-only-fail-under\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-19T21:20:24.369Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-19T21:20:24.369Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\",\"createdById\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}]}]}}
