   M: \"description\": \"Compatibility alias for brain_query with keyword=true. Lexical keyword search across the brain\n--- internal/cli/mcp.go #3  HEAD=1L MAIN=1L\n   H: \"description\": \"Compatibility alias for brain_query with semantic=true: vector search over facts and docs (and\n   M: \"description\": \"Compatibility alias for brain_query: semantic retrieval was removed (BM25 lexical matched or b\n--- internal/cli/refresh.go #1  HEAD=4L MAIN=1L\n   H: refreshOpts.seed.agent = defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, opts.Runner, repoDir)\n   M: refreshOpts.seed.agent = resolveRefreshAgentAnnounced(ctx, opts.Runner, repoDir, refreshOpts.seed.model, cmd.E\n--- internal/cli/refresh.go #2  HEAD=15L MAIN=14L\n   H: // defaultRefreshAgent picks the agent that will read session transcripts.\n   M: // defaultRefreshAgent resolves `--agent auto`.\n--- internal/cli/refresh.go #3  HEAD=26L MAIN=11L\n   H: // Ollama is preferred ONLY when a model is actually named.\n   M: // Prefer the detected harness ONLY IF its binary is runnable. Detection\n--- internal/cli/refresh.go #4  HEAD=12L MAIN=80L\n   H: // ollamaModelMissingWarning is the line a caller prints when ollama is present\n   M: // detectedAgentHarness names the agent harness THIS process is running under,\n--- internal/cli/semantic.go #1  HEAD=9L MAIN=9L\n   H: // Carried for the stream scanner, which stamps a header the provider could\n   M: // The GATE reads worktreeGateIgnore, not the `ignore` the indexer uses\n--- internal/cli/semantic.go #2  HEAD=29L MAIN=2L\n   H: // The provider could not stamp its own provenance, and brain supplied\n   M: if err := validateLiveSemanticHeader(header, head, tree, repoDir, indexOpts.worktree && dirty); err != nil {\n--- internal/cli/semantic.go #3  HEAD=38L MAIN=14L\n   H: if semanticProviderMissing(detail) {\n   M: binary := strings.TrimSpace(graphBinary)\n--- internal/cli/semantic.go #4  HEAD=92L MAIN=1L\n   H: //\n   M: func validateLiveSemanticHeader(header semanticHeader, commit, tree,