{"parentUuid":"5b42625a-c53e-46f2-9100-801f332c454e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01XU8NRgP6qTq1XUxubv4tWL","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"978eb24c-e6dc-4362-8bdb-6c7c51e35d98","timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:12:20.397Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"978eb24c-e6dc-4362-8bdb-6c7c51e35d98","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgMH2FdNyyBdn5tXMjpFZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AJrGxyRxQ7omQgs8fw6Z24","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial review PR 442","model":"opus","prompt":"Adversarially review entireio/entire-brain PR #442 (branch claude/inspiring-wright-68270a). Worktree ALREADY created for you: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/rev442 (branch rev442). Work only there. Do NOT push, do NOT merge, do NOT commit.\n\nCONTEXT\n- PR #442 claims to fix COR-2175: the `entire-brain workspace watch --distill` tick launched `memory worker --once` DETACHED, then ran a refresh needing the same brain `write.lock`; the worker held it 12-25s, refresh's 10s timeout lost, the whole tick aborted, so gated distill ran 3 times in 20 days.\n- Its fix (watch.go + watch_test.go only, +428/-11): (1) move the reconcile/launch step to AFTER the refresh via a deferred closure with a ran-guard; (2) `watchRefreshWithLockRetry` retries ONLY on lock-timeout errors, 3 retries at 15s/30s/60s, each capped at --interval, ctx-cancellable; (3) if all attempts lose the lock but an earlier successful refresh left distill/seed pending within one --distill-every window, run the pending gated work anyway with the refresh cursor left unadvanced.\n- All CI is green. Entire Gates agent review found no blocking issues. I need an INDEPENDENT skeptical read before approving.\n\nALREADY RULED OUT (do not re-derive): the previous attempt at this bug (PR #426) tried to POLL the write lock after launching the worker; that is a measured no-op (settle returned in 379us while the worker takes the lock at ~50ms) because `launchDetachedSelf` returns at `command.Start()`. #442 does NOT do that.\n\nWHAT I NEED YOU TO ATTACK — default to \"this is broken\" and only retreat when you cannot reproduce a problem:\n1. Does the reconcile step STILL run exactly once on EVERY exit path of watchTick (early return, no-change, consolidation-deferred, refresh failure, ctx cancel, panic/defer ordering)? Find any path where it now runs ZERO times or TWICE. Read the real control flow, don't trust the PR body.\n2. Does moving reconcile after refresh break anything that depended on the old ordering (e.g. refresh consuming state the reconcile produces, or the worker needing to be launched before the tick's cursor advances)? Check `internal/cli/watch.go` and the workspace fan-out path `runWorkspaceWatchPass` too — does the fan-out get the same fix or is it left racing?\n3. The retry: 15+30+60 = 105s of sleeping inside a tick. What happens when --interval is SHORTER than the waits (the per-wait cap)? Can ticks pile up / overlap? Is the ctx the right one? Can this starve the workspace fan-out (N repos x 105s)?\n4. The \"pending gated work survives a lost lock\" path: can it run distill/seed against STALE or PARTIAL state because the refresh never succeeded? Is the staleness bound actually enforced, or can an arbitrarily old successful refresh authorize it?\n5. The error classifier: does it correctly and ONLY match lock timeouts? Would it swallow a real failure (e.g. a wrapped error whose text happens to contain \"brain_locked:\")? Would it MISS a lock timeout shape that actually occurs?\n6. The nine new tests in watch_test.go: VERIFY BY WEAKENING. For each guard that matters, patch the production code to reintroduce the bug and prove the test goes RED. Report any test that stays GREEN under a weakening (an unfailable test). This is the highest-value part of the review - do it for at least: reconcile-runs-once-on-each-path, the retry schedule, the no-retry-for-non-lock-errors case, and the pending-work staleness bound.\n\nENVIRONMENT RULES (violating these produces false results):\n- This shell exports FORCE_COLOR=3 which breaks colour-assert tests. Always run tests as: `env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test ./internal/cli/ -p 1 -parallel 1 -run '<Regex>' -count=1`\n- CPU discipline: NEVER run the full suite. Scope with -run. Max GOMAXPROCS=2.\n- Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n- Use rtk-proxied commands where available (the hook rewrites git etc. automatically).\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. No prose paragraphs, no restating the PR. Just:\nVERDICT: SAFE-TO-MERGE | FIX-FIRST | REJECT\nThen a numbered list, one line each: `<file>:<line> — <defect> — <concrete failure scenario> — <evidence: command + observed output>`.\nThen a WEAKENING TABLE: `<guard> | <weakening applied> | RED or GREEN`. GREEN = unfailable test = report it.\nThen DEAD-ENDS: one line each for attacks you tried that did NOT reproduce (so I don't repeat them).\nCite file:line for everything. A claim with no command behind it is a hypothesis - label it as such."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":142715,"output_tokens":3946,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3946,"cache_read_input_tokens":142715,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AJrGxyRxQ7omQgs8fw6Z24":{"description":"Adversarial review PR 442","model":"opus","prompt":"Adversarially review entireio/entire-brain PR #442 (branch claude/inspiring-wright-68270a). Worktree ALREADY created for you: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/rev442 (branch rev442). Work only there. Do NOT push, do NOT merge, do NOT commit.\n\nCONTEXT\n- PR #442 claims to fix COR-2175: the `entire-brain workspace watch --distill` tick launched `memory worker --once` DETACHED, then ran a refresh needing the same brain `write.lock`; the worker held it 12-25s, refresh's 10s timeout lost, the whole tick aborted, so gated distill ran 3 times in 20 days.\n- Its fix (watch.go + watch_test.go only, +428/-11): (1) move the reconcile/launch step to AFTER the refresh via a deferred closure with a ran-guard; (2) `watchRefreshWithLockRetry` retries ONLY on lock-timeout errors, 3 retries at 15s/30s/60s, each capped at --interval, ctx-cancellable; (3) if all attempts lose the lock but an earlier successful refresh left distill/seed pending within one --distill-every window, run the pending gated work anyway with the refresh cursor left unadvanced.\n- All CI is green. Entire Gates agent review found no blocking issues. I need an INDEPENDENT skeptical read before approving.\n\nALREADY RULED OUT (do not re-derive): the previous attempt at this bug (PR #426) tried to POLL the write lock after launching the worker; that is a measured no-op (settle returned in 379us while the worker takes the lock at ~50ms) because `launchDetachedSelf` returns at `command.Start()`. #442 does NOT do that.\n\nWHAT I NEED YOU TO ATTACK — default to \"this is broken\" and only retreat when you cannot reproduce a problem:\n1. Does the reconcile step STILL run exactly once on EVERY exit path of watchTick (early return, no-change, consolidation-deferred, refresh failure, ctx cancel, panic/defer ordering)? Find any path where it now runs ZERO times or TWICE. Read the real control flow, don't trust the PR body.\n2. Does moving reconcile after refresh break anything that depended on the old ordering (e.g. refresh consuming state the reconcile produces, or the worker needing to be launched before the tick's cursor advances)? Check `internal/cli/watch.go` and the workspace fan-out path `runWorkspaceWatchPass` too — does the fan-out get the same fix or is it left racing?\n3. The retry: 15+30+60 = 105s of sleeping inside a tick. What happens when --interval is SHORTER than the waits (the per-wait cap)? Can ticks pile up / overlap? Is the ctx the right one? Can this starve the workspace fan-out (N repos x 105s)?\n4. The \"pending gated work survives a lost lock\" path: can it run distill/seed against STALE or PARTIAL state because the refresh never succeeded? Is the staleness bound actually enforced, or can an arbitrarily old successful refresh authorize it?\n5. The error classifier: does it correctly and ONLY match lock timeouts? Would it swallow a real failure (e.g. a wrapped error whose text happens to contain \"brain_locked:\")? Would it MISS a lock timeout shape that actually occurs?\n6. The nine new tests in watch_test.go: VERIFY BY WEAKENING. For each guard that matters, patch the production code to reintroduce the bug and prove the test goes RED. Report any test that stays GREEN under a weakening (an unfailable test). This is the highest-value part of the review - do it for at least: reconcile-runs-once-on-each-path, the retry schedule, the no-retry-for-non-lock-errors case, and the pending-work staleness bound.\n\nENVIRONMENT RULES (violating these produces false results):\n- This shell exports FORCE_COLOR=3 which breaks colour-assert tests. Always run tests as: `env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test ./internal/cli/ -p 1 -parallel 1 -run '<Regex>' -count=1`\n- CPU discipline: NEVER run the full suite. Scope with -run. Max GOMAXPROCS=2.\n- Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n- Use rtk-proxied commands where available (the hook rewrites git etc. automatically).\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. No prose paragraphs, no restating the PR. Just:\nVERDICT: SAFE-TO-MERGE | FIX-FIRST | REJECT\nThen a numbered list, one line each: `<file>:<line> — <defect> — <concrete failure scenario> — <evidence: command + observed output>`.\nThen a WEAKENING TABLE: `<guard> | <weakening applied> | RED or GREEN`. GREEN = unfailable test = report it.\nThen DEAD-ENDS: one line each for attacks you tried that did NOT reproduce (so I don't repeat them).\nCite file:line for everything. A claim with no command behind it is a hypothesis - label it as such."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"da975e28-d660-4e32-8e5f-6cbcae1f17d9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMH2F9MrtmMu2DcBSjpM","requestRef":"6c402be4-4bdf-4778-ade5-fe2f8b5f0bf8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"04fe8443-d31a-4238-9815-a159d86bdaf4","timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:12:20.396Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"04fe8443-d31a-4238-9815-a159d86bdaf4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgMH2FdNyyBdn5tXMjpFZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FPUxRd3mg4Ls9maYgEXiRK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial review PR 440","model":"opus","prompt":"Adversarially review entireio/entire-brain PR #440 (branch fix/distill-cache-salt-agent-independent). Worktree ALREADY created for you: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/rev440 (branch rev440). Work only there. Do NOT push, do NOT merge, do NOT commit.\n\nCONTEXT\n- PR #440 (+505/-28, files: internal/cli/distill_cmd.go, internal/cli/distill_cache_salt_test.go, internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go) claims: the distill cache salt hashed agent+model+effort alongside the prompt/reconcile-prompt/threshold, so the setup backfill (`--agent codex --effort low`) and the session-end hook (auto, no effort) never shared a cache entry and each re-paid the agent for sessions the other had already distilled. Measured: a real 289-session brain reported 0 cached bare vs 72 cached with `--agent codex --effort low`.\n- Its fix: `distillCacheSalt` now covers only prompt-with-taxonomy + reconcile prompt + confidence threshold + preprocessing version. Entries written by older binaries under the agent-bearing formula are \"grandfathered\" against an ENUMERATED set of known producer salts (current run's own, plus codex and claude-code with/without effort low and a pinned model, in both preprocessing versions) and rewritten under the new salt on first sight. Same grandfathering applied to the checkpoint fast path, the file-era-to-checkpoint content migration, and the per-chunk reuse cache.\n\nCRITICAL INVARIANT YOU MUST TEST AGAINST (this is the thing that makes this class of change dangerous):\nA chunk or session WRONGLY believed already-distilled is a chunk whose facts NEVER get written. Losing memories is strictly worse than paying the agent twice. Also note: facts in this product are BRANCH-PARTITIONED on disk (`factsBranchRelDir(branch)` -> `facts/<slug>-<sha>/facts.ndjson`), and the cache key is `branch/discriminator/session` (see distill_cmd.go around line 2440). A previous attempt at a neighbouring ticket died because it reused cache entries ACROSS branches, which marks the destination branch done while that branch's facts file stays EMPTY.\n\nWHAT I NEED YOU TO ATTACK — default to \"this is broken\", retreat only when you cannot reproduce:\n1. Can the new salt collide two genuinely different extraction configurations into one cache entry, so a session is skipped whose facts were produced under materially different instructions? Enumerate exactly what the old salt covered and what the new one drops, and for each dropped input decide whether it changes the FACTS produced (legitimate to drop) or only who produced them (legitimate to drop) — be specific.\n2. The grandfathering enumeration: it hardcodes a finite set of legacy producer salts. Can a legacy entry written by a producer NOT in that set be matched anyway (false positive -> skipped session -> lost facts)? Can the rewrite step clobber a DIFFERENT session's entry (key collision during the rewrite)?\n3. Does the grandfathering respect branch partitioning, or does any of it match across branches/discriminators? Check the chunk-reuse grandfathering especially. Trace the actual key construction.\n4. Duplicate session ids: there is existing code that refuses to grandfather when a session id is duplicated across exports (`duplicateKeys` in distill_cmd.go). Does the new grandfathering honour that guard, or does it reintroduce the bug the guard exists to prevent?\n5. The checkpoint fast path and the file-era-to-checkpoint content migration: does grandfathering there change which facts get written, or only whether the agent is called?\n6. VERIFY BY WEAKENING — highest-value part. For each new test (TestDistillCacheSaltIgnoresAgentModelEffort, TestDistillGrandfathersAgentSaltedCacheEntries, TestLegacyAgentDistillCacheSaltsEnumerateKnownProducers, TestDistillGrandfathersAgentSaltedCheckpointEntries, TestDistillChunkDoneUnderLegacySalt, TestDistillDryRunPredictsCacheAccurately), patch the PRODUCTION code to reintroduce the defect the test names and prove it goes RED. Report any test that stays GREEN (unfailable test).\n7. Does any test assert a helper directly while the CALL SITE ignores that helper? (That exact shape shipped a bug here before.) Check that each guard drives the real call path.\n\nENVIRONMENT RULES (violating these produces false results):\n- This shell exports FORCE_COLOR=3 which breaks colour-assert tests. Always run tests as: `env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=2 go test ./internal/cli/ -p 1 -parallel 1 -run '<Regex>' -count=1`\n- CPU discipline: NEVER run the full suite. Scope with -run. Max GOMAXPROCS=2.\n- Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n- Use rtk-proxied commands where available.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. No prose paragraphs, no restating the PR. Just:\nVERDICT: SAFE-TO-MERGE | FIX-FIRST | REJECT\nThen numbered: `<file>:<line> — <defect> — <concrete failure scenario, naming which facts are lost> — <evidence: command + observed output>`.\nThen WEAKENING TABLE: `<guard> | <weakening applied> | RED or GREEN`.\nThen DEAD-ENDS: attacks tried that did NOT reproduce, one line each.\nCite file:line for everything. Label any unverified claim as a hypothesis."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":142715,"output_tokens":3946,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3946,"cache_read_input_tokens